1
00:01:53,945 --> 00:01:56,472
[train horn blaring]

2
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:04,035
[song begins]

3
00:02:14,228 --> 00:02:20,048
<i>♪ A pinch of night ♪</i>

4
00:02:21,059 --> 00:02:27,526
<i>♪ A drop of day ♪</i>

5
00:02:27,859 --> 00:02:34,372
<i>♪ They dissolve into the holy Ganga ♪</i>

6
00:02:34,777 --> 00:02:40,990
<i>♪ And become Kashi ♪</i>

7
00:02:41,553 --> 00:02:46,666
<i>♪ This sacred stream flows without end ♪</i>

8
00:02:46,789 --> 00:02:50,089
<i>♪ And this holy city speaks in whispers ♪</i>

9
00:02:50,228 --> 00:02:57,142
<i>♪ Kashi, so comforting,
like a beloved at night ♪</i>

10
00:03:10,802 --> 00:03:17,202
<i>♪ A lonely woman, like a boat ♪</i>

11
00:03:17,654 --> 00:03:23,651
<i>♪ Floats across Ganga at night ♪</i>

12
00:03:23,652 --> 00:03:30,995
<i>♪ Was it towards daybreak ♪</i>

13
00:03:31,363 --> 00:03:36,456
<i>♪ That she disappeared like the moon? ♪</i>

14
00:03:36,751 --> 00:03:41,482
<i>♪ Are you a misty winter sky? ♪</i>

15
00:03:41,483 --> 00:03:48,357
<i>♪ Is she Umadevi
going to Kashi from Kaveri? ♪</i>

16
00:03:48,358 --> 00:03:51,475
<i>♪ An indelible illution, the Maya? ♪</i>

17
00:03:51,476 --> 00:03:58,343
<i>♪ Who is this like the smile of the Sun,
the red-rayed? ♪</i>

18
00:03:58,344 --> 00:04:04,517
<i>♪ Who is this like the wind of
southern hill ranges? ♪</i>

19
00:04:05,204 --> 00:04:13,818
<i>♪ Who is this, like a village rivulet? ♪</i>

20
00:04:46,296 --> 00:04:53,063
<i>♪ Who are you? ♪</i>

21
00:04:53,227 --> 00:05:05,837
<i>♪ The wandering,
unshaken lamp's flame from the Aarti? ♪</i>

22
00:05:06,381 --> 00:05:12,668
<i>♪ Or the cloud sent by the Sahya forest? ♪</i>

23
00:05:13,128 --> 00:05:16,419
<i>♪ Are you the boatman of twilight ♪</i>

24
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:19,185
<i>♪ To those
who come hoping to cross the river? ♪</i>

25
00:05:19,186 --> 00:05:24,318
<i>♪ The one who revolves around
the high ghats of dawn and dusk ♪</i>

26
00:05:24,319 --> 00:05:26,217
<i>♪ Like gentle sunshine? ♪</i>

27
00:05:26,218 --> 00:05:29,527
<i>♪ O Tathagata? ♪</i>

28
00:05:29,694 --> 00:05:36,920
<i>♪ Are you Shiva,
who reigns upon the white mountain? ♪</i>

29
00:05:37,784 --> 00:05:44,424
<i>♪ Or the one who waters the entire earth? ♪</i>

30
00:05:44,639 --> 00:05:50,470
<i>♪ Who are you? ♪</i>

31
00:05:50,471 --> 00:05:57,959
<i>♪ Who is this,
like the purest form of wisdom? ♪</i>

32
00:06:06,946 --> 00:06:09,099
[temple bells ringing]

33
00:06:13,338 --> 00:06:16,044
[ambient background noise]

34
00:06:28,437 --> 00:06:32,897
'CHINNA CHINNA AASAI'

35
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,974
[soft music playing]

36
00:06:42,005 --> 00:06:44,265
[boat engine rumbling]

37
00:06:51,798 --> 00:06:53,267
Hello, Master ji.

38
00:06:53,485 --> 00:06:54,875
Hello! Hello!

39
00:06:54,876 --> 00:06:57,516
Come on. Let me give you a round.

40
00:06:57,517 --> 00:06:58,805
Not now.

41
00:06:59,293 --> 00:07:01,380
[melodious flute playing]

42
00:07:04,096 --> 00:07:05,378
Yes.

43
00:07:05,379 --> 00:07:08,048
In ten minutes. I'll be there.
I've reached Prabhu Ghat.

44
00:07:08,264 --> 00:07:10,906
Aren't you near the hotel?
I'll come there.

45
00:07:10,907 --> 00:07:12,352
Are you done for today?

46
00:07:13,203 --> 00:07:14,805
Not yet.

47
00:07:14,806 --> 00:07:16,204
One more round is pending.

48
00:07:20,253 --> 00:07:21,565
Shall we have tea?

49
00:07:21,688 --> 00:07:23,024
Why not? Come.

50
00:07:23,309 --> 00:07:25,248
[humming a tune]

51
00:07:30,735 --> 00:07:31,853
Two cups of tea.

52
00:07:31,854 --> 00:07:33,223
So what's up, Master ji?

53
00:07:33,224 --> 00:07:34,523
Doing good. How about you?

54
00:07:34,727 --> 00:07:36,055
All good here too.

55
00:07:36,907 --> 00:07:39,167
[ambient background noise]

56
00:07:40,309 --> 00:07:41,278
Here's your tea.

57
00:07:43,821 --> 00:07:45,055
And here's yours.

58
00:07:48,362 --> 00:07:50,676
Oh, I forgot to tell you.

59
00:07:50,677 --> 00:07:53,292
That lady sitting there
has been crying for some time now.

60
00:07:53,667 --> 00:07:55,300
I asked her but she's not answering.

61
00:07:55,792 --> 00:07:57,761
I think she's from your part of the country.

62
00:07:57,909 --> 00:07:59,355
Please check on her.

63
00:08:06,570 --> 00:08:08,450
[soft music playing]

64
00:08:10,761 --> 00:08:11,996
Please ask her once.

65
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:23,381
Hello? What happened?

66
00:08:29,876 --> 00:08:31,165
Are you a Tamilian?

67
00:08:37,634 --> 00:08:38,907
What happened?

68
00:08:42,946 --> 00:08:43,986
Oh-no...

69
00:08:43,987 --> 00:08:46,574
[soft music playing]

70
00:08:50,914 --> 00:08:53,360
The folks who travelled in your boat,

71
00:08:53,469 --> 00:08:54,923
were they Tamilians?

72
00:08:54,924 --> 00:08:56,419
<i>No.</i>

73
00:08:56,664 --> 00:08:58,051
I see.

74
00:08:59,202 --> 00:09:01,815
There's a lady at the Ghat here.

75
00:09:02,084 --> 00:09:04,300
She got separated from her group.

76
00:09:04,301 --> 00:09:05,672
<i>Oh, really?</i>

77
00:09:06,329 --> 00:09:08,389
<i>I'll let you know if I get any info
about her group.</i>

78
00:09:08,594 --> 00:09:09,985
Alright. Okay.

79
00:09:18,321 --> 00:09:19,735
Alright, Master ji.

80
00:09:21,399 --> 00:09:24,563
Bag and phone snatching is
quite common here.

81
00:09:25,138 --> 00:09:27,146
No use in filing a complaint.

82
00:09:27,993 --> 00:09:29,954
Don't you even know your own phone number?

83
00:09:32,295 --> 00:09:34,201
Phone numbers of any of your family members?

84
00:09:37,390 --> 00:09:40,617
Maybe the address or phone number of
the hotel you're staying in?

85
00:09:43,737 --> 00:09:45,792
We should be a bit more careful, right?

86
00:09:47,765 --> 00:09:48,859
Master ji,

87
00:09:49,625 --> 00:09:51,148
there's a temple nearby.

88
00:09:51,453 --> 00:09:53,457
Lots of Tamil folks visit that temple.

89
00:09:53,458 --> 00:09:54,950
Maybe go check there?

90
00:09:59,297 --> 00:10:01,610
He was talking about
checking at a nearby temple.

91
00:10:01,938 --> 00:10:03,367
What happened, madam?

92
00:10:04,446 --> 00:10:06,008
Is the tea not good?

93
00:10:07,126 --> 00:10:09,743
This is Lord Bholenath's town.

94
00:10:09,744 --> 00:10:12,096
Somebody gets lost here every day.

95
00:10:12,215 --> 00:10:13,324
Right, Master ji?

96
00:10:15,946 --> 00:10:17,048
Have your tea.

97
00:10:17,143 --> 00:10:19,390
[mellow music playing]

98
00:10:46,374 --> 00:10:48,281
[temple bells ringing]

99
00:10:50,035 --> 00:10:52,840
No travel groups visited here today,
he said.

100
00:10:54,816 --> 00:10:56,356
Don't worry. Let's search for them.

101
00:10:56,357 --> 00:10:57,463
I mean, look for them.

102
00:10:57,464 --> 00:10:59,589
- We're hungry. Please help us.
- Go away. Go.

103
00:10:59,590 --> 00:11:02,856
Please give us something to eat.
We're hungry.

104
00:11:05,113 --> 00:11:06,191
Three cups of tea.

105
00:11:07,199 --> 00:11:08,465
I'm taking a biscuit packet.

106
00:11:10,558 --> 00:11:12,004
Biscuits too?

107
00:11:13,558 --> 00:11:14,808
For me?

108
00:11:15,199 --> 00:11:16,668
Take one more.

109
00:11:17,982 --> 00:11:19,922
[mellow music playing]

110
00:11:20,199 --> 00:11:21,847
Did you eat anything?

111
00:11:23,601 --> 00:11:25,967
[ambient street restaurant noise]

112
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:35,315
[soft music playing]

113
00:12:01,578 --> 00:12:03,227
Can I trust you?

114
00:12:07,086 --> 00:12:08,523
Can I trust you?

115
00:12:17,338 --> 00:12:18,600
[PA system announcement]

116
00:12:18,601 --> 00:12:19,939
What happened? You didn't leave?

117
00:12:25,125 --> 00:12:27,156
There's this Kishen Bhai's restaurant nearby.

118
00:12:28,070 --> 00:12:30,046
They serve nice south Indian breakfast.

119
00:12:31,336 --> 00:12:32,820
Are you from Madras?

120
00:12:35,625 --> 00:12:37,531
All south Indians are 'Madrasis' here.

121
00:12:38,695 --> 00:12:40,054
Well, where's is your hometown?

122
00:12:42,132 --> 00:12:43,452
Near Tanjavur.

123
00:12:43,453 --> 00:12:45,859
I see! Nagavally's hometown!

124
00:12:47,507 --> 00:12:49,164
Tanjavur dolls!

125
00:12:49,523 --> 00:12:51,007
I have one in my home.

126
00:12:51,858 --> 00:12:54,038
I bought it when I visited Tanjavur
back in 1982.

127
00:12:54,039 --> 00:12:55,601
It's a mesmerizing place.

128
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:57,382
Move this side.

129
00:13:02,632 --> 00:13:04,078
When did you reach Varanasi?

130
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:06,250
Today morning.

131
00:13:07,290 --> 00:13:09,868
Any idea which side your hotel is?

132
00:13:10,117 --> 00:13:11,507
Or how far it is from here?

133
00:13:13,796 --> 00:13:14,976
No idea.

134
00:13:15,906 --> 00:13:17,781
There was a temple nearby that hotel.

135
00:13:22,624 --> 00:13:25,155
How did you get separated
from your tour package team?

136
00:13:28,218 --> 00:13:29,968
Never mind. Come.

137
00:13:33,551 --> 00:13:35,224
[melodious music playing]

138
00:13:43,554 --> 00:13:45,039
Please come. This is the place.

139
00:13:45,281 --> 00:13:46,977
Hello, Master!

140
00:13:46,978 --> 00:13:47,953
Hello, ji!

141
00:13:47,954 --> 00:13:49,937
- How are you?
- All good.

142
00:13:49,938 --> 00:13:51,297
You came with your wife today?

143
00:13:51,298 --> 00:13:53,121
- Oh-no! She's not my wife.
- Not your wife?

144
00:13:53,659 --> 00:13:55,471
It's okay. Please come.

145
00:13:55,577 --> 00:13:56,804
Please come.

146
00:14:00,232 --> 00:14:01,466
Please take a seat.

147
00:14:05,536 --> 00:14:07,380
Hey kiddo, go take their order.

148
00:14:12,038 --> 00:14:15,093
Don't get him wrong.
I've come here only with my daughter.

149
00:14:15,094 --> 00:14:16,772
That's why he asked that.

150
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,024
What do you wanna eat?

151
00:14:23,174 --> 00:14:24,916
Is Masala Dosa okay for you?

152
00:14:26,891 --> 00:14:29,383
Masala Dosa, and two cups of tea.
Masala tea.

153
00:14:34,906 --> 00:14:38,477
If you have any idea about the places
you were planning to visit,

154
00:14:38,478 --> 00:14:39,992
we could go there and look for them.

155
00:14:41,056 --> 00:14:43,196
I understand Malayalam a bit.

156
00:14:43,197 --> 00:14:44,932
That makes it easier.

157
00:14:45,185 --> 00:14:46,842
Let me ask you then.

158
00:14:46,843 --> 00:14:50,179
Do you remember when your return train is?

159
00:14:50,743 --> 00:14:52,439
It's tomorrow morning's train.

160
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:54,423
It's easy then. We can find them easily.

161
00:14:57,315 --> 00:15:00,964
Well, I mean if we can't find them
even after looking for them here.

162
00:15:04,365 --> 00:15:05,607
Here's your tea.

163
00:15:06,545 --> 00:15:07,998
What's your name?

164
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:10,897
Leela.

165
00:15:10,898 --> 00:15:13,599
Leela? Special tea for you.

166
00:15:17,013 --> 00:15:19,529
Varanasi tea is the real deal.

167
00:15:20,162 --> 00:15:22,732
I drink minimum five cups every day.

168
00:15:23,395 --> 00:15:25,215
I don't drink tea.

169
00:15:28,031 --> 00:15:29,711
What's the big deal if five turns six?

170
00:15:32,129 --> 00:15:34,955
[melodious music playing]

171
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:39,218
Who's there in your family now?

172
00:15:40,562 --> 00:15:43,180
It's been one and a half years
since he passed.

173
00:15:45,735 --> 00:15:46,954
Kids?

174
00:15:47,312 --> 00:15:48,719
I have a son.

175
00:15:49,969 --> 00:15:51,204
What does he do?

176
00:15:57,532 --> 00:15:59,634
There's a Tamil association office nearby.

177
00:15:59,950 --> 00:16:01,622
Let's go there and inform them.

178
00:16:02,095 --> 00:16:05,563
There's a chance that your group may
go there and enquire about you.

179
00:16:05,845 --> 00:16:07,127
Have your food.

180
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:09,800
[soft music playing]

181
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:17,648
There's a significant connection between
Tamil Nadu and Varanasi.

182
00:16:17,801 --> 00:16:19,463
Do you know that?

183
00:16:20,383 --> 00:16:23,149
I think it was in the 15th century...

184
00:16:23,457 --> 00:16:26,222
Parakrama Pandyan, the king of Madurai

185
00:16:26,453 --> 00:16:29,108
wanted to build
a majestic Shiva temple there--

186
00:16:29,109 --> 00:16:30,614
Can we leave from here soon?

187
00:16:31,498 --> 00:16:32,600
Shall we leave?

188
00:16:33,864 --> 00:16:36,426
We'll waste our time if we keep speaking.
Please eat your food.

189
00:16:40,272 --> 00:16:42,486
[ambient noise at ghat]

190
00:16:49,770 --> 00:16:51,223
I have informed them.

191
00:16:52,131 --> 00:16:54,514
They've received no enquiries yet.

192
00:16:58,298 --> 00:16:59,532
Let's see how it goes.

193
00:17:08,664 --> 00:17:10,867
If you're tired,
do you wanna go sit at their office?

194
00:17:11,383 --> 00:17:13,906
There's a chance that
your group comes there looking for you.

195
00:17:22,312 --> 00:17:24,734
Ganga Aarti ceremony happens here
in the evening.

196
00:17:25,055 --> 00:17:27,297
They will definitely come here to see that.

197
00:17:27,828 --> 00:17:29,359
We can go look for them there.

198
00:17:32,953 --> 00:17:34,180
It's a bit difficult.

199
00:17:34,181 --> 00:17:37,234
But it's better than looking for them
without any idea where they are.

200
00:17:41,873 --> 00:17:43,140
This is the person.

201
00:17:43,141 --> 00:17:44,169
Hello.

202
00:17:44,170 --> 00:17:46,162
Do you have any problem
if she waits here?

203
00:17:46,163 --> 00:17:47,292
As long as she wants!

204
00:17:47,293 --> 00:17:49,612
I'm not carrying her, right?
It's the earth that'll bear her weight.

205
00:17:49,613 --> 00:17:51,293
Take your honourable seat!

206
00:17:51,431 --> 00:17:53,118
I'll go look for them.

207
00:17:53,435 --> 00:17:55,568
Be seated. Please don't go anywhere.

208
00:17:56,648 --> 00:17:58,217
Please sit, madam.

209
00:18:06,937 --> 00:18:09,150
[soft humorous music playing]

210
00:18:16,497 --> 00:18:17,927
Tanjavur?

211
00:18:22,572 --> 00:18:23,736
Leela.

212
00:18:24,384 --> 00:18:25,634
Your father...

213
00:18:25,853 --> 00:18:27,736
gave you a nice name, isn't it?

214
00:18:28,962 --> 00:18:31,173
Well, why do you look so glum?

215
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:33,275
Your face looks so dull.

216
00:18:34,170 --> 00:18:35,767
Be enthusiastic.

217
00:18:36,556 --> 00:18:38,322
You definitely have a backstory.

218
00:18:38,323 --> 00:18:39,742
You don't have to share it immediately.

219
00:18:39,743 --> 00:18:43,579
Shall I tell you my backstory
to close the distance?

220
00:18:46,845 --> 00:18:48,343
At my village, Paravakottai,

221
00:18:48,344 --> 00:18:49,953
I worked hard all alone,

222
00:18:50,322 --> 00:18:52,040
and became a big millionaire.

223
00:18:52,751 --> 00:18:55,103
As I worked hard to earn all my wealth,

224
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,189
only I know the value of that money.

225
00:18:57,587 --> 00:19:01,243
So, I'd ask my wife about
how she spends the money I gave her,

226
00:19:01,368 --> 00:19:03,798
and if my son asks for money,
I'd ask them why he needs it.

227
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:05,587
They apparently didn't like it.

228
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:07,892
So one day,

229
00:19:08,072 --> 00:19:10,611
they planned to kill me
while I was asleep.

230
00:19:10,751 --> 00:19:13,556
That broke my heart,
and I decided to end my life,

231
00:19:13,947 --> 00:19:16,868
I came to Varanasi,
and jumped into the holy river Ganga.

232
00:19:17,431 --> 00:19:18,813
Suddenly,

233
00:19:18,814 --> 00:19:22,251
Lord Kashi Vishwanath held me close,
pulled me out from water, and told me,

234
00:19:22,558 --> 00:19:26,121
"A woman from your birthplace Tanjavur
will come seeking you,

235
00:19:26,566 --> 00:19:28,807
I will make you and her unite,

236
00:19:28,808 --> 00:19:31,441
live the rest of your life with her!"

237
00:19:31,631 --> 00:19:34,897
You're that woman from Tanjavur
who Lord Kashi Vishwanath mentioned--

238
00:19:47,316 --> 00:19:48,738
I didn't know about him.

239
00:19:49,050 --> 00:19:50,449
Did he trouble you a lot?

240
00:20:02,090 --> 00:20:03,652
Don't mind them.

241
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:05,787
Do it like that.

242
00:20:06,502 --> 00:20:07,941
Do it like that.

243
00:20:07,942 --> 00:20:10,162
[melodious music playing]

244
00:20:12,629 --> 00:20:14,621
I heard they eat corpses.

245
00:20:14,957 --> 00:20:16,098
Is that true?

246
00:20:16,487 --> 00:20:19,729
I've heard that
they eat half-cremated bodies.

247
00:20:22,901 --> 00:20:25,135
That guy is a fraud.
It's evident from his looks.

248
00:20:26,832 --> 00:20:28,746
This place is not like
what I expected it to be.

249
00:20:30,656 --> 00:20:31,796
What?

250
00:20:32,179 --> 00:20:33,570
This Varanasi?

251
00:20:36,507 --> 00:20:40,241
Just look around,
the way you want to see Varanasi.

252
00:20:40,499 --> 00:20:42,890
Then you will see the true Varanasi.

253
00:20:43,570 --> 00:20:46,385
Only those who deserve this land
will understand that.

254
00:20:46,386 --> 00:20:49,353
[soft humming]

255
00:21:39,257 --> 00:21:45,962
<i>♪ Unleash the rain, O beloved ♪</i>

256
00:21:47,387 --> 00:21:55,963
<i>♪ Unleash the rain, O beloved ♪</i>

257
00:21:56,538 --> 00:22:01,448
<i>♪ Unleash the rain, O beloved ♪</i>

258
00:22:11,423 --> 00:22:15,001
Some people attach coins to the corpses
as a passage fee to the other world.

259
00:22:15,264 --> 00:22:16,615
Those boys are in search of that.

260
00:22:16,814 --> 00:22:18,853
Would God charge for that too?

261
00:22:20,107 --> 00:22:22,849
It's okay.
Ultimately the ones who deserve get it.

262
00:22:23,616 --> 00:22:24,624
I didn't understand.

263
00:22:24,625 --> 00:22:26,744
Uncle, please buy it.

264
00:22:26,745 --> 00:22:28,892
- I don't want it.
- Please buy it!

265
00:22:29,030 --> 00:22:30,349
Please!

266
00:22:30,903 --> 00:22:32,942
Please buy it, uncle!

267
00:22:33,498 --> 00:22:34,546
Do you want it?

268
00:22:34,547 --> 00:22:36,077
Please buy it!

269
00:22:37,771 --> 00:22:39,217
Please buy one!

270
00:22:39,218 --> 00:22:41,029
Shall I buy one then?

271
00:22:46,952 --> 00:22:48,005
Okay.

272
00:22:48,006 --> 00:22:50,386
[mellow music playing]

273
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:03,882
Why are you doing me such favours?

274
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:10,693
You didn't tell me anything about you.

275
00:23:11,575 --> 00:23:13,137
Well, you never asked me.

276
00:23:14,506 --> 00:23:15,748
'You', with respect.

277
00:23:16,675 --> 00:23:18,605
Sorry. 'You'.

278
00:23:21,049 --> 00:23:22,190
So tell me.

279
00:23:24,424 --> 00:23:26,307
I am Madhavan Master.

280
00:23:26,877 --> 00:23:28,776
A retired upper primary school teacher.

281
00:23:29,612 --> 00:23:31,284
I have a daughter. Janaki.

282
00:23:31,502 --> 00:23:34,502
She's doing Kathak masters
at Banaras university.

283
00:23:35,752 --> 00:23:37,940
I often come here to meet her.

284
00:23:39,744 --> 00:23:40,800
Dance?

285
00:23:40,801 --> 00:23:42,213
Yes. Why?

286
00:23:47,307 --> 00:23:48,706
How about your wife?

287
00:23:49,932 --> 00:23:51,956
She gave me Janaki and left.

288
00:23:56,260 --> 00:23:57,471
Manikandan.

289
00:23:58,010 --> 00:24:00,229
The son of his first wife.

290
00:24:01,909 --> 00:24:04,722
After two years of
Manikandan's mother's demise,

291
00:24:04,723 --> 00:24:06,565
his father married me.

292
00:24:07,502 --> 00:24:08,917
Do you stay with Manikandan?

293
00:24:08,918 --> 00:24:09,971
No.

294
00:24:11,010 --> 00:24:13,010
He lives in Delhi with his family.

295
00:24:14,174 --> 00:24:15,721
He works as an engineer there.

296
00:24:18,791 --> 00:24:20,565
I have a grandson.

297
00:24:21,206 --> 00:24:22,346
His name is Rohit.

298
00:24:22,440 --> 00:24:23,980
He studies in first standard.

299
00:24:23,981 --> 00:24:26,507
[soft music playing]

300
00:24:29,586 --> 00:24:32,023
It's been quite long since I met him.

301
00:24:34,268 --> 00:24:36,198
Everybody's quite busy, you know?

302
00:24:40,401 --> 00:24:41,643
What to say?

303
00:24:42,909 --> 00:24:44,323
If you look at it that way,

304
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:47,294
this too gives me peace of mind
in a way.

305
00:24:50,098 --> 00:24:51,449
But we can't always

306
00:24:52,235 --> 00:24:54,126
be in peace, right?

307
00:25:00,151 --> 00:25:02,143
You came here for sightseeing, right?

308
00:25:03,653 --> 00:25:05,098
I can help you if you want.

309
00:25:06,785 --> 00:25:08,160
You're here anyway.

310
00:25:10,011 --> 00:25:11,699
We have to look for them,

311
00:25:11,785 --> 00:25:13,543
and we have time till Ganga Aarti.

312
00:25:15,618 --> 00:25:17,384
You can even pay me a guide's fee.

313
00:25:17,544 --> 00:25:19,224
[soft music playing]

314
00:25:19,428 --> 00:25:21,913
If it's okay with you,
I shall show you something.

315
00:25:22,707 --> 00:25:24,457
You can decide after that.

316
00:25:29,092 --> 00:25:31,415
If you don't like it,
you can go sit at the office.

317
00:25:38,133 --> 00:25:40,008
[pigeons fluttering]

318
00:25:40,781 --> 00:25:42,563
[soothing melody begins]

319
00:25:52,529 --> 00:26:03,344
<i>♪ Is there a soul that never soars high? ♪</i>

320
00:26:03,874 --> 00:26:13,563
<i>♪ There are answers to
every hardship in life ♪</i>

321
00:26:14,196 --> 00:26:17,586
<i>♪ My sky and my earth become one ♪</i>

322
00:26:17,587 --> 00:26:23,506
<i>♪ And I rise above, wings unfolding ♪</i>

323
00:26:24,864 --> 00:26:26,749
<i>♪ Is this reality, or an illusion? ♪</i>

324
00:26:26,750 --> 00:26:28,263
<i>♪ Though this life may be a fleeting lie ♪</i>

325
00:26:28,264 --> 00:26:32,539
<i>♪ Your care and affection feel true
And they have shown me who I am ♪</i>

326
00:26:47,537 --> 00:26:48,944
[anklets jingling]

327
00:26:49,530 --> 00:26:51,077
[footsteps]

328
00:26:55,373 --> 00:26:57,342
[indistinct chatter and giggling]

329
00:27:01,254 --> 00:27:03,514
Didn't we see them there too?

330
00:27:05,094 --> 00:27:06,101
Yes.

331
00:27:08,599 --> 00:27:11,301
Looks like their whole life
is inside the phone.

332
00:27:13,367 --> 00:27:15,607
Don't just blame the phone entirely.

333
00:27:16,288 --> 00:27:17,908
It does have its uses.

334
00:27:24,327 --> 00:27:26,746
Do you know every place in Varanasi?

335
00:27:28,152 --> 00:27:29,166
Yes.

336
00:27:29,659 --> 00:27:30,666
Almost.

337
00:27:32,527 --> 00:27:34,033
Can I ask you something?

338
00:27:37,017 --> 00:27:39,630
Subbu had told me...

339
00:27:40,013 --> 00:27:44,213
we get Lassi, Malaiyo, and hot Kachoris here.

340
00:27:44,603 --> 00:27:46,366
What brought you here, actually?

341
00:27:46,944 --> 00:27:48,295
[gentle music playing]

342
00:27:51,272 --> 00:27:52,764
[pigeons fluttering]

343
00:27:55,367 --> 00:27:57,235
Am I...

344
00:27:58,756 --> 00:28:00,062
...talking too much?

345
00:28:06,772 --> 00:28:08,209
[pigeons flapping]

346
00:28:09,459 --> 00:28:11,334
[grains scattering]

347
00:28:15,834 --> 00:28:17,758
Have you travelled like this before?

348
00:28:19,647 --> 00:28:23,271
I've gone to Delhi
a couple of times with him,

349
00:28:23,379 --> 00:28:24,699
for his treatment.

350
00:28:26,321 --> 00:28:27,894
Where all have you travelled?

351
00:28:28,741 --> 00:28:30,294
To a few places here and there.

352
00:28:33,701 --> 00:28:35,549
Of all the places you've been,

353
00:28:35,550 --> 00:28:37,750
which did you like the most?

354
00:28:40,134 --> 00:28:42,261
Last July, I went to Spiti.

355
00:28:43,634 --> 00:28:44,970
I loved it.

356
00:28:47,201 --> 00:28:48,207
Where is that?

357
00:28:50,014 --> 00:28:51,936
It's a village in Himachal.

358
00:28:53,027 --> 00:28:55,581
The whole journey there
is so beautiful, you know?

359
00:28:58,177 --> 00:28:59,457
Himachal...

360
00:29:01,401 --> 00:29:03,448
It must be full of ‘pani' there, right?

361
00:29:06,054 --> 00:29:07,061
'Pani'?

362
00:29:08,394 --> 00:29:09,686
'Pani' means…

363
00:29:12,687 --> 00:29:13,694
Snow.

364
00:29:13,881 --> 00:29:15,085
Ah, snow?

365
00:29:15,272 --> 00:29:16,859
Not during that time.

366
00:29:17,086 --> 00:29:18,479
I'm planning to go this March.

367
00:29:18,967 --> 00:29:21,047
My son-in-law is coming from the UK.

368
00:29:21,161 --> 00:29:23,002
We're all planning together.

369
00:29:26,264 --> 00:29:28,084
[gentle music continues]

370
00:29:28,807 --> 00:29:29,867
Will you come along?

371
00:29:31,030 --> 00:29:32,741
[motorcycle passing]

372
00:29:35,534 --> 00:29:37,526
I don't even know where the others went!

373
00:29:37,527 --> 00:29:38,556
No idea.

374
00:29:41,967 --> 00:29:43,029
[soft laughter]

375
00:29:43,030 --> 00:29:44,334
[pigeons flapping]

376
00:29:46,101 --> 00:29:48,656
Didn't you say you wanted to have Lassi?

377
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:49,794
Let's go.

378
00:29:50,094 --> 00:29:51,127
Okay.

379
00:29:52,311 --> 00:29:53,772
[traffic noise]

380
00:29:56,764 --> 00:29:58,108
[pleasant music playing]

381
00:30:08,153 --> 00:30:09,160
Here you go.

382
00:30:10,116 --> 00:30:11,191
[bicycle bell rings]

383
00:30:11,192 --> 00:30:14,048
At this age, I worry such things
might cause health issues.

384
00:30:14,218 --> 00:30:16,534
Was that meant for me,

385
00:30:16,535 --> 00:30:18,282
or for you?

386
00:30:19,369 --> 00:30:21,795
Don't worry. I have this regularly.

387
00:30:23,159 --> 00:30:24,603
But it isn't blue in colour!

388
00:30:25,116 --> 00:30:27,123
[background traffic noise]

389
00:30:36,086 --> 00:30:38,280
I'm trusting you and drinking this.

390
00:30:40,397 --> 00:30:41,959
[playful rhythmic music playing]

391
00:30:46,293 --> 00:30:47,829
- How is it?
- Not bad!

392
00:30:50,821 --> 00:30:53,339
Still, nothing like Tanjavur Ashoka halwa.

393
00:30:54,289 --> 00:30:56,099
That's truly special.

394
00:30:56,206 --> 00:30:58,633
My grandmother used to make it so well.

395
00:30:59,533 --> 00:31:01,796
Every time I eat it, I'm reminded of her.

396
00:31:03,720 --> 00:31:06,454
She lived happily till ninety.

397
00:31:07,100 --> 00:31:09,959
And one day, smiling,
she just went to sleep.

398
00:31:14,254 --> 00:31:16,474
This doesn't come anywhere close
to Ashoka halwa.

399
00:31:16,674 --> 00:31:18,411
That's all I meant to say.

400
00:31:20,214 --> 00:31:22,712
You haven't tried Kozhikode halwa,
have you?

401
00:31:23,373 --> 00:31:24,412
No.

402
00:31:24,413 --> 00:31:26,812
Try it once… it'll sail across your mouth!

403
00:31:30,420 --> 00:31:31,686
[vomiting]

404
00:31:31,687 --> 00:31:32,983
[Leela chuckles]

405
00:31:33,452 --> 00:31:34,584
[Madhavan panting]

406
00:31:34,717 --> 00:31:35,881
[vomiting continues]

407
00:31:38,022 --> 00:31:39,381
[music continues]

408
00:31:47,571 --> 00:31:49,643
Now do you see who's really old?

409
00:31:51,498 --> 00:31:53,709
[children chattering and playing]

410
00:31:59,632 --> 00:32:01,224
Sister, please buy this lamp.

411
00:32:01,225 --> 00:32:02,564
It's only ten rupees.

412
00:32:02,565 --> 00:32:04,083
- Ten rupees.
- No, no.

413
00:32:04,084 --> 00:32:05,642
Only ten rupees, please buy it.

414
00:32:05,643 --> 00:32:07,109
Take two for ten.

415
00:32:08,003 --> 00:32:09,009
Come here for a second.

416
00:32:11,555 --> 00:32:12,929
Hold this, hold this.

417
00:32:15,809 --> 00:32:17,420
- Please buy it, sister?
- No, dear.

418
00:32:17,909 --> 00:32:18,915
Please, buy it.

419
00:32:19,742 --> 00:32:20,749
What is it?

420
00:32:21,021 --> 00:32:22,028
Please, buy it.

421
00:32:22,342 --> 00:32:23,349
Ask him.

422
00:32:23,929 --> 00:32:25,633
- Brother, buy a lamp?
- No, no, not now.

423
00:32:25,634 --> 00:32:26,988
After arati, the evening rituals, maybe.

424
00:32:26,989 --> 00:32:28,691
- Two for ten!
- Not now, go on.

425
00:32:28,692 --> 00:32:29,713
Please, just ten rupees.

426
00:32:29,714 --> 00:32:31,781
Can you give me a hundred rupees?

427
00:32:32,322 --> 00:32:34,466
Two for ten, please buy them.

428
00:32:36,276 --> 00:32:37,306
Buy them.

429
00:32:37,307 --> 00:32:38,308
Here you go.

430
00:32:38,309 --> 00:32:39,717
No, I don't want money.

431
00:32:39,718 --> 00:32:42,419
If you want to buy the lamp, buy it.
Otherwise, leave it.

432
00:32:42,868 --> 00:32:43,875
Huh?

433
00:32:47,056 --> 00:32:49,020
Didn't she just say something really smart?

434
00:32:49,768 --> 00:32:50,901
Yes.

435
00:32:52,809 --> 00:32:55,324
She must want to study too, right?

436
00:32:56,209 --> 00:32:57,707
How far did you study?

437
00:32:59,669 --> 00:33:01,701
I didn't even pass tenth grade.

438
00:33:01,949 --> 00:33:02,956
Aha!

439
00:33:03,436 --> 00:33:05,393
Most kids working here dropped out

440
00:33:05,394 --> 00:33:07,816
only because they couldn't afford school.

441
00:33:09,616 --> 00:33:10,622
Poor things.

442
00:33:11,234 --> 00:33:13,256
If only she had someone to support her…

443
00:33:13,854 --> 00:33:15,640
Are you thinking of taking her with you?

444
00:33:16,844 --> 00:33:18,975
If she's okay, I'm okay.

445
00:33:18,976 --> 00:33:20,320
[Madhavan laughs softly]

446
00:33:21,650 --> 00:33:24,569
Keep track of everything,
I'll pay you back later.

447
00:33:26,991 --> 00:33:28,491
[kite flapping]

448
00:33:30,902 --> 00:33:32,480
When does the evening ritual start?

449
00:33:32,829 --> 00:33:34,422
At 6 in the evening.

450
00:33:35,398 --> 00:33:37,187
[indistinct chatter]

451
00:33:43,016 --> 00:33:44,263
My daughter had called.

452
00:33:44,264 --> 00:33:45,599
Let me call her back.

453
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:49,491
[footsteps]

454
00:33:50,804 --> 00:33:52,257
[gentle classical music playing]

455
00:34:23,903 --> 00:34:33,485
<i>♪ You fill every breath of mine ♪</i>

456
00:34:34,092 --> 00:34:38,579
<i>♪ Like a gentle fragrance ♪</i>

457
00:34:39,237 --> 00:34:44,350
<i>♪ Like the warmth of love ♪</i>

458
00:34:44,882 --> 00:34:49,882
<i>♪ O Krishna, eternal guardian of hearts ♪</i>

459
00:34:50,080 --> 00:34:56,000
<i>♪ My soul calls out to you, come ♪</i>

460
00:34:56,836 --> 00:35:02,045
<i>♪ This is your Radha ♪</i>

461
00:35:02,046 --> 00:35:07,136
<i>♪ This is your Meera ♪</i>

462
00:35:07,137 --> 00:35:12,401
<i>♪ This is your Gopika ♪</i>

463
00:35:12,402 --> 00:35:18,757
<i>♪ This is your Radhika ♪</i>

464
00:35:39,521 --> 00:35:43,127
<i>♪ You dwell in my breath ♪</i>

465
00:35:43,464 --> 00:35:47,904
<i>♪ You are my body and my soul ♪</i>

466
00:35:49,183 --> 00:35:53,413
<i>♪ I am the river that flows beside you ♪</i>

467
00:35:53,414 --> 00:35:58,429
<i>♪ And you are the rhythm
that moves through me ♪</i>

468
00:35:58,572 --> 00:36:02,096
<i>♪ My restless mind ♪</i>

469
00:36:02,097 --> 00:36:04,665
<i>♪ My yearning eyes ♪</i>

470
00:36:04,666 --> 00:36:08,922
<i>♪ They wander through the night
in search of you ♪</i>

471
00:36:30,125 --> 00:36:34,689
<i>♪ I am your Radha ♪</i>

472
00:36:34,690 --> 00:36:39,803
<i>♪ You are my Ghanshyam ♪</i>

473
00:36:39,804 --> 00:36:44,792
<i>♪ Our names are one ♪</i>

474
00:36:44,930 --> 00:36:50,217
<i>♪ Our names are one ♪</i>

475
00:36:50,811 --> 00:36:55,877
<i>♪ Come closer,
listen to the yearnings of my soul ♪</i>

476
00:36:56,073 --> 00:37:02,173
<i>♪ O Krishna, eternal guardian of hearts ♪</i>

477
00:37:02,813 --> 00:37:08,071
<i>♪ This is your Radha ♪</i>

478
00:37:08,072 --> 00:37:13,149
<i>♪ This is your Meera ♪</i>

479
00:37:13,150 --> 00:37:18,416
<i>♪ This is your Gopika ♪</i>

480
00:37:18,417 --> 00:37:24,829
<i>♪ This is your Radhika ♪</i>

481
00:37:26,292 --> 00:37:28,385
[child mimics car engine]
[damaru beats]

482
00:37:29,201 --> 00:37:30,962
Didn't you say someone came asking?

483
00:37:31,349 --> 00:37:33,001
There was one more lady with us, right?

484
00:37:33,002 --> 00:37:34,443
Why didn't you go along with her?

485
00:37:34,831 --> 00:37:35,991
Ear cleaning...

486
00:37:36,515 --> 00:37:37,941
- Sir, you wanna clean your ears?
- What?

487
00:37:37,942 --> 00:37:39,302
- Get your ears cleaned once.
- Go away, man!

488
00:37:39,549 --> 00:37:42,508
- Always bugging people!
- Why do these folks come to Varanasi?!

489
00:37:42,829 --> 00:37:45,548
If you'd kept an eye on that lady,
this wouldn't have happened.

490
00:37:45,549 --> 00:37:47,632
Yeah yeah, that's our job, right?

491
00:37:47,633 --> 00:37:51,263
Before you leave, at least try
to find out where she went.

492
00:37:51,367 --> 00:37:53,549
This is all they do,
sitting around gossiping!

493
00:37:53,684 --> 00:37:55,811
Name... Leela.

494
00:37:56,548 --> 00:37:57,779
Age?

495
00:37:57,894 --> 00:37:59,174
Fifty... fifty-two.

496
00:37:59,316 --> 00:38:00,968
Place?

497
00:38:00,969 --> 00:38:02,813
Tanjavur, Tamil Nadu.

498
00:38:02,814 --> 00:38:04,030
Tanjavur...

499
00:38:05,062 --> 00:38:06,269
Tamil Nadu.

500
00:38:06,621 --> 00:38:08,148
That's it, details done.

501
00:38:09,128 --> 00:38:11,862
[faint announcements in distance]

502
00:38:13,190 --> 00:38:14,268
[microphone tapping]

503
00:38:14,269 --> 00:38:15,330
Hello? Hello?

504
00:38:15,331 --> 00:38:16,890
Hope they heard that.

505
00:38:16,891 --> 00:38:18,628
[over PA]
Mic check, one two three.

506
00:38:18,629 --> 00:38:20,584
<i>Attention please, missing person alert.</i>

507
00:38:20,585 --> 00:38:23,957
Don't panic. If nothing works out,
we'll check at the station tomorrow.

508
00:38:24,289 --> 00:38:25,844
A woman named Leela...

509
00:38:26,322 --> 00:38:28,065
52 years old...

510
00:38:28,408 --> 00:38:30,883
<i>From Tanjavur, Tamil Nadu,
seems to have lost her way here.</i>

511
00:38:31,090 --> 00:38:33,800
<i>If anyone has any information,
please inform the help desk.</i>

512
00:38:33,801 --> 00:38:35,888
Do you think they're really looking for me?

513
00:38:41,008 --> 00:38:43,465
Did you have other plans for today?

514
00:38:45,061 --> 00:38:46,541
Oh!

515
00:38:49,919 --> 00:38:51,592
Can you do me a favour?

516
00:38:52,019 --> 00:38:53,502
I need to buy a sari for Janaki.

517
00:38:53,503 --> 00:38:55,019
It's her birthday tomorrow.

518
00:38:55,445 --> 00:38:56,971
But I don't know how to pick one.

519
00:38:57,526 --> 00:38:58,932
[chuckles]

520
00:38:59,972 --> 00:39:01,423
You're asking me that?

521
00:39:01,926 --> 00:39:03,329
I'm from Tanjavur, after all!

522
00:39:04,539 --> 00:39:05,843
Subbu always says...

523
00:39:06,279 --> 00:39:08,352
My fashion sense is top class.

524
00:39:08,979 --> 00:39:10,659
[both chuckle]

525
00:39:10,892 --> 00:39:12,386
Who's this Subbu?

526
00:39:12,959 --> 00:39:14,677
I must meet her!

527
00:39:16,516 --> 00:39:18,826
You won't get to, whenever you want.

528
00:39:19,266 --> 00:39:22,759
She comes down from Hyderabad
only once in six months.

529
00:39:23,106 --> 00:39:24,630
She's my neighbour's daughter-in-law.

530
00:39:25,252 --> 00:39:26,791
But to me,

531
00:39:28,264 --> 00:39:29,730
she's more like a little sister.

532
00:39:30,612 --> 00:39:32,375
Even this Varanasi trip

533
00:39:32,376 --> 00:39:34,305
she's the one who arranged it for me.

534
00:39:34,911 --> 00:39:35,918
Okay, okay.

535
00:39:36,899 --> 00:39:39,212
The shop is a bit far from here.

536
00:39:39,459 --> 00:39:40,466
But we don't have to walk.

537
00:39:42,251 --> 00:39:44,298
In that case, I have a small wish...

538
00:39:45,136 --> 00:39:46,651
[calm music playing]

539
00:39:47,612 --> 00:39:49,347
[cycle rickshaw bell rings]

540
00:39:54,128 --> 00:39:55,784
[uplifting music playing]

541
00:40:23,324 --> 00:40:30,057
<i>♪ O desire, are you too the river ♪</i>

542
00:40:31,362 --> 00:40:37,628
<i>♪ That caresses the shore ♪</i>

543
00:40:38,686 --> 00:40:48,711
<i>♪ Without spilling over? ♪</i>

544
00:40:49,531 --> 00:40:58,033
<i>♪ You seem like a lonely path,
aching with endless distances ♪</i>

545
00:40:58,820 --> 00:41:08,400
<i>♪ Who is the tender cloud
drizzling upon your sorrow ♪</i>

546
00:41:09,064 --> 00:41:17,003
<i>♪ Like a dream? ♪</i>

547
00:41:39,072 --> 00:41:57,386
<i>♪ Who are you, like the divine form of
Goddess Gowri adorned with new leaves? ♪</i>

548
00:41:57,387 --> 00:42:01,554
<i>♪ Who, so near to me ♪</i>

549
00:42:01,555 --> 00:42:18,631
<i>♪ Like the starlit sky over Mount Kailash? ♪</i>

550
00:42:56,630 --> 00:42:58,879
<i>♪ I do not know... ♪</i>

551
00:42:58,880 --> 00:43:02,331
<i>♪ Tell me, without drifting away
like a river ♪</i>

552
00:43:02,332 --> 00:43:08,076
<i>♪ Are you the goddess-heart
that bleeds for the whole world? ♪</i>

553
00:43:08,077 --> 00:43:10,336
<i>♪ Are you Lalitha (the gentle Goddess)
or Jwalitha (the blazing one)? ♪</i>

554
00:43:10,337 --> 00:43:15,367
<i>♪ O, maiden of pure spring waters... ♪</i>

555
00:43:15,368 --> 00:43:17,668
You'll wear out your sandals
walking that fast.

556
00:43:18,944 --> 00:43:21,555
The saree you picked for Janaki was nice.

557
00:43:23,286 --> 00:43:25,719
Look, a call from the Tamil Association.

558
00:43:27,391 --> 00:43:28,926
Sorry, I was just…

559
00:43:29,751 --> 00:43:30,803
They're just jasmine flowers, right?

560
00:43:30,804 --> 00:43:32,213
Not rose or anything.

561
00:43:33,232 --> 00:43:34,638
That… sorry, I…

562
00:43:34,639 --> 00:43:36,006
I didn't like it.

563
00:43:36,378 --> 00:43:37,901
It felt a bit odd.

564
00:43:38,524 --> 00:43:40,616
Jasmine suits the saree so well.

565
00:43:40,989 --> 00:43:42,743
That's why I…
[Phone rings]

566
00:43:48,982 --> 00:43:50,663
One minute, my daughter's calling.

567
00:43:55,742 --> 00:43:56,749
Hello?

568
00:43:57,469 --> 00:43:58,710
Hello.

569
00:43:58,711 --> 00:44:00,802
I was at a dance shoot, missed your call.

570
00:44:00,896 --> 00:44:01,902
Where's Dad?

571
00:44:02,036 --> 00:44:03,365
I'm at the ghat.

572
00:44:03,969 --> 00:44:05,460
Aren't you coming here?

573
00:44:05,829 --> 00:44:06,836
No.

574
00:44:07,296 --> 00:44:08,683
Then I'll come there.

575
00:44:09,096 --> 00:44:10,387
Dad, you didn't eat, right?

576
00:44:10,508 --> 00:44:11,647
Let's eat together.

577
00:44:11,648 --> 00:44:13,684
I'll be there in 30 minutes.

578
00:44:15,556 --> 00:44:17,548
I... I'm here with a friend.

579
00:44:17,549 --> 00:44:18,763
<i>Which friend?</i>

580
00:44:18,871 --> 00:44:20,111
From our hometown.

581
00:44:20,316 --> 00:44:21,450
Which friend back home?

582
00:44:21,675 --> 00:44:23,276
You wouldn't know even if I told you.

583
00:44:24,082 --> 00:44:25,402
A friend of yours I don't know?

584
00:44:26,076 --> 00:44:28,209
That... um...

585
00:44:29,654 --> 00:44:30,661
Um… fine.

586
00:44:31,028 --> 00:44:32,512
What am I supposed to do now?

587
00:44:33,315 --> 00:44:34,659
We're going to eat.

588
00:44:35,076 --> 00:44:36,602
Then I'll come there.

589
00:44:37,202 --> 00:44:38,568
We can eat together.

590
00:44:39,322 --> 00:44:41,048
No need. He'll leave in the evening.

591
00:44:41,049 --> 00:44:42,571
After that I'll come to the hostel.

592
00:44:42,856 --> 00:44:44,466
Um… okay.

593
00:44:45,629 --> 00:44:47,279
Don't forget your medicine after food.

594
00:44:47,708 --> 00:44:48,715
I'll call you then.

595
00:44:49,094 --> 00:44:51,416
And did you arrange tomorrow's thing?

596
00:44:52,275 --> 00:44:54,655
Oh, I forgot it.

597
00:44:55,308 --> 00:44:57,557
Huh?! Really?

598
00:44:57,558 --> 00:44:59,053
<i>I'll go soon after this.</i>

599
00:44:59,600 --> 00:45:01,047
Uhm… fine.

600
00:45:01,316 --> 00:45:02,322
- I'm hanging up.
- Okay.

601
00:45:11,176 --> 00:45:13,589
We need to go somewhere. Shall we?

602
00:45:15,976 --> 00:45:18,275
It's to arrange something for tomorrow.

603
00:45:18,421 --> 00:45:19,955
It was urgent.

604
00:45:20,235 --> 00:45:21,688
I completely forgot.

605
00:45:22,376 --> 00:45:24,562
Only remembered when my daughter asked.

606
00:45:24,982 --> 00:45:27,049
Say sorry to me.

607
00:45:27,262 --> 00:45:28,269
Oh?

608
00:45:29,342 --> 00:45:30,349
Say “sorry.”

609
00:45:30,616 --> 00:45:31,622
Sorry!

610
00:45:33,816 --> 00:45:34,822
Shall we go?

611
00:45:35,169 --> 00:45:36,176
Let's go.

612
00:45:37,190 --> 00:45:39,644
[Islamic call to prayer]

613
00:45:40,559 --> 00:45:42,036
O, Lord Murugan...!

614
00:45:43,282 --> 00:45:45,782
If you want, we can rest for a while.

615
00:45:46,479 --> 00:45:48,261
Yes. I was about to ask you the same.

616
00:45:48,262 --> 00:45:49,776
Alright. Let's go sit there.

617
00:46:04,908 --> 00:46:06,533
Is your health okay?

618
00:46:06,705 --> 00:46:07,814
Yes.

619
00:46:08,182 --> 00:46:09,635
I've got a slight blood pressure issue.

620
00:46:10,407 --> 00:46:11,420
Why?

621
00:46:12,307 --> 00:46:13,815
Nothing. I just asked.

622
00:46:15,212 --> 00:46:16,031
[glass shattering, baby crying]

623
00:46:16,032 --> 00:46:18,166
You've turned my home to hell!

624
00:46:18,315 --> 00:46:20,425
You've ruined my peace of mind!
Always ranting!

625
00:46:20,426 --> 00:46:22,885
What am I ranting?
I'm the one who's in stress, right?

626
00:46:23,002 --> 00:46:24,502
You neither cook, nor do anything else!

627
00:46:24,768 --> 00:46:26,330
- Loser!
- What? Huh?

628
00:46:26,690 --> 00:46:28,993
Go to your loser friends now!

629
00:46:28,994 --> 00:46:30,429
They'll serve you food!

630
00:46:30,430 --> 00:46:31,557
[door shutting]

631
00:46:31,883 --> 00:46:33,647
[motorcycle engine revving]

632
00:46:33,648 --> 00:46:35,270
[baby crying]

633
00:46:36,338 --> 00:46:39,651
Have you and your wife ever had
such serious fights?

634
00:46:40,752 --> 00:46:42,299
Well, no.

635
00:46:43,698 --> 00:46:46,221
We were together for only a year and a half.

636
00:46:46,700 --> 00:46:48,165
[soft humming]

637
00:46:48,166 --> 00:46:49,565
To be frank,

638
00:46:50,432 --> 00:46:51,862
some six or seven months.

639
00:46:53,299 --> 00:46:54,721
But that time,

640
00:46:55,244 --> 00:46:56,690
it was full of fun.

641
00:46:59,377 --> 00:47:00,526
Then she got pregnant,

642
00:47:00,527 --> 00:47:01,636
her parents took her home,

643
00:47:01,637 --> 00:47:03,452
she delivered our child,
and all hell broke loose.

644
00:47:03,996 --> 00:47:05,709
[humming continues]

645
00:47:15,143 --> 00:47:17,619
Me and my husband used to fight
quite often.

646
00:47:19,377 --> 00:47:20,916
Even for trivial matters,

647
00:47:21,151 --> 00:47:22,838
we used to fight.

648
00:47:26,096 --> 00:47:27,276
Even then,

649
00:47:27,277 --> 00:47:29,033
I love him a lot.

650
00:47:29,326 --> 00:47:31,373
[soft music playing]

651
00:47:32,323 --> 00:47:36,510
On the other hand, he never had
any love or affection towards me.

652
00:47:43,823 --> 00:47:45,541
Rather than a wife,

653
00:47:46,143 --> 00:47:49,237
he needed a maid
who could take care of his son.

654
00:47:51,658 --> 00:47:53,830
I was the only one who couldn't realize it.

655
00:47:58,182 --> 00:48:00,221
Even when he was at the hospital,

656
00:48:01,080 --> 00:48:03,885
he used to tell me that
taking care of him is my duty.

657
00:48:11,627 --> 00:48:14,377
What's the point in discussing
all these, right?

658
00:48:16,158 --> 00:48:18,323
Your Malayalam is quite good.

659
00:48:19,416 --> 00:48:23,057
Keep that 'dam' issue aside,
and we're all one.

660
00:48:27,682 --> 00:48:30,040
You said you wanted to go somewhere
urgently, right?

661
00:48:30,041 --> 00:48:31,151
- Yes.
- Shall we go?

662
00:48:31,152 --> 00:48:32,166
Sure.

663
00:48:33,083 --> 00:48:34,890
[soft music playing]

664
00:48:35,467 --> 00:48:37,077
Hello, Master ji. How are you?

665
00:48:37,078 --> 00:48:38,452
Hello. All good.

666
00:48:39,170 --> 00:48:41,155
- I have a guest with me today.
- Who is she?

667
00:48:41,256 --> 00:48:42,467
Is she from your village?

668
00:48:42,608 --> 00:48:43,858
Hello. Hello.

669
00:48:44,983 --> 00:48:46,756
Isn't everything on track for tomorrow?

670
00:48:47,303 --> 00:48:50,272
Khalid, aren't the preparations for
tomorrow's veg meals done?

671
00:48:50,538 --> 00:48:51,788
Yes.

672
00:48:53,405 --> 00:48:56,022
It's already 1 o' clock.
Shall we eat biryani from here?

673
00:48:56,483 --> 00:48:58,178
Mutton biryani is so yummy here.

674
00:48:58,314 --> 00:48:59,627
Do you eat mutton?

675
00:49:00,032 --> 00:49:01,625
[soft music playing]

676
00:49:08,653 --> 00:49:10,755
Come on, Papa. Let's play.

677
00:49:10,756 --> 00:49:12,193
Not now, dear. I've got lot of work to do.

678
00:49:12,194 --> 00:49:14,013
- Please come.
- No dear, I'm working now.

679
00:49:14,014 --> 00:49:16,357
Later, okay?
Go play with your brother now.

680
00:49:16,358 --> 00:49:17,990
He's not ready to play with me.

681
00:49:17,991 --> 00:49:19,199
Here's tomatoes.

682
00:49:19,200 --> 00:49:20,625
I'm too tired.

683
00:49:24,382 --> 00:49:25,804
One second.

684
00:49:26,958 --> 00:49:28,083
Hello?

685
00:49:28,458 --> 00:49:30,246
Did you not leave, Dad?
What happened?

686
00:49:30,247 --> 00:49:34,028
A lady here got lost from her tour group.

687
00:49:34,292 --> 00:49:36,896
I felt bad for her and decided to help her.

688
00:49:37,091 --> 00:49:38,263
I'm with her now.

689
00:49:38,356 --> 00:49:41,106
I'll come there after helping her
to reach her tour group.

690
00:49:42,153 --> 00:49:43,834
My dear Madhavan Master.

691
00:49:43,835 --> 00:49:45,373
Why do you need to give me an explanation?

692
00:49:45,374 --> 00:49:46,661
Don't I know you?

693
00:49:47,200 --> 00:49:49,372
<i>Even if you say that you guys are in love,
I'm okay with that.</i>

694
00:49:49,544 --> 00:49:51,216
Stop it, you!

695
00:49:52,130 --> 00:49:55,528
I swear. If I find her to be okay,
I shall get you guys married.

696
00:49:57,114 --> 00:49:59,255
I'm hanging up, okay?
I called you to tell you this.

697
00:49:59,256 --> 00:50:00,248
Don't hang up!

698
00:50:00,249 --> 00:50:01,333
What's it?

699
00:50:01,843 --> 00:50:05,773
You're not the one who would worry about
what I'd think, and cook up a lie.

700
00:50:06,630 --> 00:50:08,302
What's going on? Anything fishy?

701
00:50:09,685 --> 00:50:11,200
Stop it, girl!

702
00:50:11,409 --> 00:50:13,355
[soft music playing]

703
00:50:25,750 --> 00:50:26,961
Wow!

704
00:50:27,117 --> 00:50:28,390
Have it.

705
00:50:29,890 --> 00:50:32,398
Only if you have someone close to you,

706
00:50:32,486 --> 00:50:33,845
the phone will be of some use.

707
00:50:34,202 --> 00:50:36,977
There are plenty of folks here
who live like they have nobody,

708
00:50:36,978 --> 00:50:38,530
even though they have everybody.

709
00:50:40,020 --> 00:50:41,778
We need to go to one more place now.

710
00:50:41,986 --> 00:50:43,166
Shall we?

711
00:50:47,202 --> 00:50:49,622
[mellow music playing]

712
00:51:09,893 --> 00:51:10,847
Hello.

713
00:51:10,848 --> 00:51:13,862
Milord! How are you, Madhav ji?

714
00:51:13,863 --> 00:51:15,346
First class. And you?

715
00:51:15,347 --> 00:51:17,174
I'm also doing fine.

716
00:51:19,349 --> 00:51:22,998
She doesn't look old enough
to get an admission here.

717
00:51:22,999 --> 00:51:24,374
She's not here for an admission.

718
00:51:24,542 --> 00:51:26,249
She's my friend. Leela.

719
00:51:26,250 --> 00:51:27,276
I see.

720
00:51:27,277 --> 00:51:28,871
She's here for some sightseeing.

721
00:51:28,872 --> 00:51:30,489
I see. Please come.

722
00:51:31,596 --> 00:51:32,901
Please come.

723
00:51:33,667 --> 00:51:36,448
For tomorrow,
aren't the arrangements done for

724
00:51:36,698 --> 00:51:38,410
fifty meals?

725
00:51:38,411 --> 00:51:39,463
Yes.

726
00:51:40,397 --> 00:51:44,329
Did you get any missing enquiries?

727
00:51:44,704 --> 00:51:47,404
Missing enquiry? What happened?

728
00:51:47,730 --> 00:51:50,304
She had come here with a tour group
from Tanjavur.

729
00:51:51,218 --> 00:51:52,805
She lost her way.

730
00:51:53,459 --> 00:51:55,979
Please call me if any enquiry comes.

731
00:51:56,192 --> 00:51:57,559
Sure.

732
00:51:58,102 --> 00:52:00,295
[melancholic music playing]

733
00:52:06,949 --> 00:52:09,755
Okay. I shall take your leave then.

734
00:52:09,756 --> 00:52:11,364
Something urgent came up.

735
00:52:11,365 --> 00:52:13,504
- See you tomorrow then. Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

736
00:52:17,813 --> 00:52:19,188
What's going on here?

737
00:52:19,868 --> 00:52:21,188
I feel strange.

738
00:52:21,501 --> 00:52:22,680
Well...

739
00:52:22,907 --> 00:52:27,047
Some people believe that
dying here can help them achieve salvation.

740
00:52:28,657 --> 00:52:31,149
Most of these people come here alone
and live here.

741
00:52:31,586 --> 00:52:33,501
Or they can have a helper too.

742
00:52:34,969 --> 00:52:38,595
If they don't die within 15 days of check-in,
they'll have to check out from here.

743
00:52:38,596 --> 00:52:40,172
That's the rule here.

744
00:52:41,532 --> 00:52:45,743
And there are some people who donate
all their wealth and stay here till death.

745
00:52:46,493 --> 00:52:50,157
Also, there are some people here
who have done their final rites themselves.

746
00:52:51,352 --> 00:52:52,571
How's that possible?

747
00:52:52,924 --> 00:52:55,096
How can they know the time of their death?

748
00:52:55,860 --> 00:52:58,016
Only God knows that, right?

749
00:52:59,477 --> 00:53:01,180
Do you know that God?

750
00:53:03,876 --> 00:53:05,819
We have so many Gods, don't we?

751
00:53:05,820 --> 00:53:07,805
You can ask me about whoever you want.

752
00:53:11,802 --> 00:53:13,756
I have only one question.

753
00:53:15,544 --> 00:53:18,606
If I see God some day,

754
00:53:20,012 --> 00:53:23,216
I want to ask him
why he gave me a life like this.

755
00:53:24,321 --> 00:53:27,040
Did I really live a good life?

756
00:53:29,003 --> 00:53:30,300
I don't know.

757
00:53:33,986 --> 00:53:37,588
I've never opened up like this
with anybody before.

758
00:53:40,113 --> 00:53:42,824
We've got time till 'Ganga Aarti' ceremony.
Keep talking.

759
00:53:46,650 --> 00:53:48,650
I feel very happy, you know?

760
00:53:49,773 --> 00:53:52,460
What makes you really happy?

761
00:53:54,074 --> 00:53:57,027
Seeing Janaki dance,

762
00:53:57,028 --> 00:53:58,503
makes me really happy.

763
00:53:59,613 --> 00:54:02,222
I too feel like meeting Janaki.

764
00:54:02,952 --> 00:54:05,257
She's an excellent dancer, isn't she?

765
00:54:08,047 --> 00:54:10,875
I too wanted to be a dance teacher once.

766
00:54:15,741 --> 00:54:18,030
I've learnt dance during my childhood.

767
00:54:19,053 --> 00:54:22,943
Before my marriage, I've danced several times
during temple festivals.

768
00:54:24,568 --> 00:54:26,553
But, after marriage...

769
00:54:27,115 --> 00:54:28,920
I danced only once.

770
00:54:29,842 --> 00:54:31,482
And he didn't like it.

771
00:54:33,498 --> 00:54:34,975
So I stopped it right then.

772
00:54:37,990 --> 00:54:41,131
Had you told me this earlier,
we could've gone to her institute.

773
00:54:41,896 --> 00:54:43,279
That's okay.

774
00:54:44,711 --> 00:54:46,306
The moment I saw you, I felt that

775
00:54:46,307 --> 00:54:48,110
there's a dancer hiding within you.

776
00:54:48,949 --> 00:54:50,293
Please don't say such things.

777
00:54:50,294 --> 00:54:51,738
I feel awkward.

778
00:54:53,030 --> 00:54:54,580
When will Ganga Aarti ceremony begin?

779
00:54:54,581 --> 00:54:56,481
It will take another 3-4 hours.

780
00:54:57,111 --> 00:54:58,971
What can we do till then?

781
00:55:00,212 --> 00:55:02,572
Subbu had told me that
the boating experience is good here.

782
00:55:04,586 --> 00:55:06,607
It's better to do the boating in the morning.

783
00:55:09,016 --> 00:55:11,483
Then... What can we do now?

784
00:55:14,501 --> 00:55:17,013
There's gonna be a 'Sitar' performance
at Kala Kendra today.

785
00:55:17,014 --> 00:55:18,060
It's quite nearby.

786
00:55:18,061 --> 00:55:19,068
Shall we go there?

787
00:55:19,614 --> 00:55:20,941
Is it? Let's go there then.

788
00:55:21,073 --> 00:55:23,093
[mellow music playing]

789
00:55:30,545 --> 00:55:32,098
[ambient noise at ghat]

790
00:55:32,099 --> 00:55:34,959
This place is peculiar in several ways.
Do you know that?

791
00:55:36,141 --> 00:55:37,938
Here, lizards don't chirp,

792
00:55:38,411 --> 00:55:39,794
dogs don't bark,

793
00:55:40,872 --> 00:55:42,442
crows don't caw,

794
00:55:42,897 --> 00:55:44,616
eagles don't circle the sky,

795
00:55:44,723 --> 00:55:46,364
all those are--

796
00:55:46,365 --> 00:55:47,674
Ouch!

797
00:55:59,269 --> 00:56:01,489
[soft, sad music playing]

798
00:56:31,407 --> 00:56:33,883
Everybody calls me ill-fated.

799
00:56:35,094 --> 00:56:38,219
Please leave me
before something bad happens to you.

800
00:56:47,089 --> 00:56:48,230
Please come.

801
00:56:49,185 --> 00:56:50,865
[temple bells ringing]

802
00:57:24,819 --> 00:57:27,757
She wasn't watching out.

803
00:57:29,388 --> 00:57:30,544
It's okay.

804
00:57:36,926 --> 00:57:38,090
It's alright.

805
00:57:47,890 --> 00:57:49,156
Shall I talk to him?

806
00:57:52,063 --> 00:57:53,227
Go ahead.

807
00:58:09,287 --> 00:58:10,748
Please forgive me.

808
00:58:23,373 --> 00:58:26,560
Isn't it so tough to travel wearing a saree?

809
00:58:28,879 --> 00:58:29,973
Isn't it?

810
00:58:31,387 --> 00:58:33,723
She hated wearing it.

811
00:58:39,207 --> 00:58:41,026
It was for our marriage that
she wore a saree.

812
00:58:44,863 --> 00:58:46,755
But it was only for a short while.

813
00:58:46,756 --> 00:58:48,318
After that, for our marriage reception,

814
00:58:48,707 --> 00:58:51,185
she wore a white and white...
I don't know that attire's name.

815
00:58:51,824 --> 00:58:53,215
She wore something like that.

816
00:58:53,527 --> 00:58:54,684
She looked so pretty in it.

817
00:58:58,137 --> 00:58:59,848
We used to travel a lot.

818
00:59:00,520 --> 00:59:01,645
After...

819
00:59:03,066 --> 00:59:05,285
After our baby's arrival,
she changed completely.

820
00:59:09,043 --> 00:59:11,082
She'd call me back to back.

821
00:59:11,551 --> 00:59:13,348
She'd get angry if I ask her about our baby.

822
00:59:13,838 --> 00:59:15,378
[soft music playing]

823
00:59:17,004 --> 00:59:18,441
As if she doesn't like the baby.

824
00:59:18,926 --> 00:59:21,241
She wouldn't let me know
even if our baby is unwell.

825
00:59:23,014 --> 00:59:26,483
I was too stressed out due to all this
as well as my work pressure...

826
00:59:26,569 --> 00:59:27,874
so one day I lost it.

827
00:59:27,986 --> 00:59:29,155
I...

828
00:59:29,546 --> 00:59:30,803
snapped at her.

829
00:59:32,991 --> 00:59:34,772
But... I didn't expect her to do this.

830
00:59:40,738 --> 00:59:42,566
I didn't know that she was unwell.

831
00:59:44,988 --> 00:59:46,777
I can't do anything now. I'm helpless.

832
00:59:50,410 --> 00:59:52,066
I just can't bear this!

833
01:00:13,090 --> 01:00:14,098
Sorry...

834
01:00:27,532 --> 01:00:29,610
[religious chanting]

835
01:00:48,076 --> 01:00:49,803
Please go and dispose the ashes.

836
01:00:54,991 --> 01:00:56,647
Come. This way.

837
01:00:59,639 --> 01:01:00,756
Walk down.

838
01:01:01,193 --> 01:01:03,566
[sad music playing]

839
01:02:27,477 --> 01:02:29,644
[phone ringing]

840
01:02:41,228 --> 01:02:42,266
Hello?

841
01:02:42,267 --> 01:02:44,916
<i>Leela's tour group was here
asking for her.</i>

842
01:02:44,917 --> 01:02:46,339
<i>They're at Gwarighat now.</i>

843
01:02:46,340 --> 01:02:47,706
<i>- Please drop her there.</i>
- Okay.

844
01:02:50,942 --> 01:02:52,810
Didn't I tell you not to worry?

845
01:02:52,811 --> 01:02:54,380
They reached there, looking for you.

846
01:02:55,172 --> 01:02:57,922
They're at Gwarighat.
Let's go there via this lane.

847
01:02:58,212 --> 01:03:00,552
[soft music playing]

848
01:03:02,488 --> 01:03:03,668
Please come.

849
01:03:04,271 --> 01:03:07,111
[ambient street noise]

850
01:04:01,462 --> 01:04:03,173
It's only a bit further this way.

851
01:04:08,318 --> 01:04:10,022
They're all waiting there.

852
01:04:17,178 --> 01:04:18,779
What happened?
Don't you feel like going to them?

853
01:04:20,289 --> 01:04:21,672
You may leave.

854
01:04:22,218 --> 01:04:24,038
I'll go alone from here.

855
01:04:24,555 --> 01:04:25,717
No, let's not do that.

856
01:04:25,718 --> 01:04:26,990
It's only a few steps away.

857
01:04:26,991 --> 01:04:28,558
I'll leave only after dropping you off.

858
01:04:30,494 --> 01:04:32,228
If you come with me...

859
01:04:34,624 --> 01:04:36,491
they'll misunderstand me.

860
01:04:37,781 --> 01:04:39,007
You're right.

861
01:04:39,282 --> 01:04:40,844
But, will you be able to go alone?

862
01:04:45,271 --> 01:04:48,857
You've helped me a lot.

863
01:04:50,172 --> 01:04:53,078
Please keep tabs of
whatever money you spent.

864
01:04:55,020 --> 01:04:56,551
Once I reach home,

865
01:04:57,390 --> 01:04:58,867
I shall pay you back.

866
01:05:02,679 --> 01:05:04,812
Thanks for all the help.

867
01:05:07,256 --> 01:05:09,229
[mellow music playing]

868
01:05:22,222 --> 01:05:24,222
[ominous music playing]

869
01:06:01,055 --> 01:06:04,350
Murugan, my Lord, my aunty got married
and moved to a new house.

870
01:06:04,442 --> 01:06:05,987
Please take good care of her.

871
01:06:06,249 --> 01:06:07,715
And…

872
01:06:07,716 --> 01:06:10,116
The fish my aunty bought for me died.

873
01:06:10,489 --> 01:06:13,022
I fed it all the rice, still it died.

874
01:06:13,402 --> 01:06:15,569
I want another fish just like it.

875
01:06:15,736 --> 01:06:18,509
One with a spot on its head,
just like that one!

876
01:06:18,702 --> 01:06:19,734
Please, please…

877
01:06:19,735 --> 01:06:22,109
- I really love my aunty and that fish.
- <i>Leelavathi…</i>

878
01:06:22,110 --> 01:06:23,899
- <i>Leela…!</i>
- She’s coming, Appa!

879
01:06:25,429 --> 01:06:26,436
Tell me, Appa.

880
01:06:27,840 --> 01:06:30,483
Haven’t seen you for a while.
Where were you, Leela, my babygirl?

881
01:06:30,484 --> 01:06:32,372
I was talking to Murugan, Appa.

882
01:06:32,373 --> 01:06:33,535
Oh, is it?

883
01:06:33,536 --> 01:06:34,642
So, what did Murugan say?

884
01:06:34,789 --> 01:06:36,401
Murugan didn’t say anything, Appa.

885
01:06:36,402 --> 01:06:37,908
I told him I want another fish.

886
01:06:37,909 --> 01:06:39,111
Is that so, dear?

887
01:06:39,112 --> 01:06:42,655
Alright. I’ll go today and
catch another one just like it, okay?

888
01:06:42,656 --> 01:06:43,662
Really?

889
01:06:43,782 --> 01:06:45,255
When are you going, Appa?

890
01:06:45,256 --> 01:06:46,921
I’ll finish some work in ten minutes…

891
01:06:46,922 --> 01:06:48,341
After that, I’ll go catch it for you.

892
01:06:48,342 --> 01:06:50,709
I won’t go home without a fish today.

893
01:06:50,882 --> 01:06:51,889
Okay, my dear.

894
01:06:55,302 --> 01:06:59,229
Appa, who’s that man with the tummy?

895
01:07:00,388 --> 01:07:02,532
Who? That one? Oh, that’s our--
[Temple bell rings]

896
01:07:02,697 --> 01:07:03,922
Wow! Prasadam!

897
01:07:04,108 --> 01:07:05,881
[anklets jingling]

898
01:07:07,944 --> 01:07:09,288
[laughs]

899
01:07:11,217 --> 01:07:12,834
[soothing music playing]

900
01:07:17,889 --> 01:07:19,358
[anklets jingling]

901
01:07:21,082 --> 01:07:24,208
Appa, when will
all the temple work be finished?

902
01:07:24,209 --> 01:07:25,215
Why, dear?

903
01:07:25,376 --> 01:07:26,382
Tell me, Appa.

904
01:07:27,095 --> 01:07:29,424
It’ll be done in a couple of weeks.

905
01:07:30,202 --> 01:07:32,396
When will we go to the big temple, Appa?

906
01:07:33,138 --> 01:07:35,331
It’s close by, isn’t it? We can go anytime.

907
01:07:35,964 --> 01:07:38,742
Then shall we go, just the two of us?

908
01:07:39,502 --> 01:07:40,509
Just you and me?

909
01:07:40,922 --> 01:07:42,568
Won’t Amma and elder brother come?

910
01:07:42,569 --> 01:07:43,576
No, Appa.

911
01:07:43,702 --> 01:07:47,076
Amma keeps finding fault
with everything I do.

912
01:07:47,447 --> 01:07:49,623
Let brother stay with Amma.

913
01:07:49,624 --> 01:07:52,185
If he comes, he’ll just hit me anyway.

914
01:07:52,186 --> 01:07:54,741
But isn’t your grandma’s house right there?

915
01:07:54,742 --> 01:07:56,205
How can your mom not come there?

916
01:07:57,596 --> 01:08:00,348
Then let’s go to a temple
far, far away, Appa.

917
01:08:01,481 --> 01:08:03,612
If it’s far away,
we’ll have to go to Kashi.

918
01:08:03,613 --> 01:08:04,774
Where’s that, Appa?

919
01:08:04,775 --> 01:08:06,695
It’s very far away, dear.

920
01:08:06,882 --> 01:08:09,028
It’ll take two or three days to get there.

921
01:08:09,029 --> 01:08:10,840
We’ll need to take a train.

922
01:08:11,309 --> 01:08:13,236
Then let’s go there, Appa!

923
01:08:13,237 --> 01:08:15,760
I really love travelling by train.

924
01:08:15,951 --> 01:08:17,246
It’ll be so much fun, right?

925
01:08:17,512 --> 01:08:19,335
But it’ll be very crowded there.

926
01:08:19,336 --> 01:08:22,049
If I lose sight of my baby Leela
in that crowd, what will I do?

927
01:08:22,516 --> 01:08:24,562
I’ll never leave you, Appa.

928
01:08:24,769 --> 01:08:26,135
I’m big Leela now.

929
01:08:26,228 --> 01:08:27,459
I can take care of myself.

930
01:08:28,675 --> 01:08:30,548
Alright, you’re big Leela now.

931
01:08:30,549 --> 01:08:32,276
Then I’ll come with you to Kashi.

932
01:08:32,429 --> 01:08:33,716
I’ll take you there, Appa.

933
01:08:33,876 --> 01:08:34,882
Okay, dear.

934
01:08:35,115 --> 01:08:36,361
Do you still want more?

935
01:08:36,675 --> 01:08:37,975
Had enough?

936
01:08:38,408 --> 01:08:39,641
Do you want some, Appa?

937
01:08:39,642 --> 01:08:40,648
Eat carefully, dear.

938
01:08:43,469 --> 01:08:44,622
Hey. Hi.

939
01:08:45,861 --> 01:08:47,161
Hello, madam.

940
01:08:47,842 --> 01:08:49,397
[temple bell ringing in distance]

941
01:08:50,942 --> 01:08:51,949
[in Hindi]
Need any help?

942
01:08:57,936 --> 01:08:58,942
[in Tamil]
Are you Tamil?

943
01:08:59,716 --> 01:09:00,722
[in Telugu]
Don’t look Telugu…

944
01:09:02,582 --> 01:09:03,589
[in Malayalam]
Malayali?

945
01:09:08,856 --> 01:09:10,022
[in Tamil]
From my hometown?

946
01:09:23,538 --> 01:09:25,069
[whistling]

947
01:09:26,028 --> 01:09:28,934
Even as countless thoughts troubled
her mind…

948
01:09:30,841 --> 01:09:33,374
the world outside kept moving on.

949
01:09:34,639 --> 01:09:35,834
[playful music playing]

950
01:09:38,826 --> 01:09:39,832
Tamil, right?

951
01:09:47,962 --> 01:09:48,969
Hello?

952
01:09:49,689 --> 01:09:50,696
Yes.

953
01:09:51,762 --> 01:09:52,769
Green saree?

954
01:09:53,582 --> 01:09:54,805
Yes, she's here.

955
01:09:57,256 --> 01:09:58,262
Nose ring?

956
01:09:59,096 --> 01:10:00,116
That too.

957
01:10:03,969 --> 01:10:05,234
But won’t say a word…

958
01:10:07,302 --> 01:10:08,309
What?

959
01:10:10,434 --> 01:10:12,077
Could she be mute?

960
01:10:14,776 --> 01:10:15,782
Hello.

961
01:10:16,716 --> 01:10:17,722
Hello.

962
01:10:21,778 --> 01:10:23,215
[footsteps]

963
01:10:28,180 --> 01:10:29,373
[pensive music playing]

964
01:10:29,374 --> 01:10:32,129
Usually, no one who ends up here ever leaves.

965
01:10:33,002 --> 01:10:35,011
They all die and vanish here.

966
01:10:36,702 --> 01:10:38,551
If you don’t want that,

967
01:10:39,195 --> 01:10:41,323
tell me what your problem is.

968
01:10:46,531 --> 01:10:48,021
[sobbing]

969
01:10:48,022 --> 01:10:50,069
Oh no! Hey, cool! Cool! Cool!

970
01:10:50,196 --> 01:10:51,202
I was just kidding!

971
01:10:52,216 --> 01:10:53,623
Don’t cry!
[Playful music]

972
01:10:54,101 --> 01:10:55,251
Ugh!

973
01:10:55,252 --> 01:10:56,258
I’m dead!

974
01:10:56,816 --> 01:10:58,677
Please, I can really help you.

975
01:10:59,546 --> 01:11:01,409
Just please, don’t cry.
Just don't cry!

976
01:11:02,476 --> 01:11:03,482
Ugh!

977
01:11:07,396 --> 01:11:10,033
JANAKI [On phone]: <i>Not everyone
can understand everyone else, Dad.</i>

978
01:11:10,929 --> 01:11:12,718
Maybe she couldn’t understand you.

979
01:11:14,876 --> 01:11:15,882
<i>But…</i>

980
01:11:16,249 --> 01:11:17,256
<i>Aunty…</i>

981
01:11:18,289 --> 01:11:21,002
Didn’t you ask
why she behaved like that, Dad?

982
01:11:23,907 --> 01:11:25,095
Whatever it is, come here.

983
01:11:25,096 --> 01:11:26,558
Don’t sit there brooding.

984
01:11:26,559 --> 01:11:27,399
Okay.

985
01:11:27,400 --> 01:11:29,582
<i>Then come now. Don’t delay it.</i>
[Phone beeps]

986
01:11:29,877 --> 01:11:30,928
One sec, dear.

987
01:11:30,929 --> 01:11:31,936
<i>Okay.</i>

988
01:11:33,485 --> 01:11:36,301
RANJITH [On phone]: <i>Hello, this is Ranjith,
Tamil team’s coordinator.</i>

989
01:11:36,302 --> 01:11:37,595
<i>Where are you?</i>

990
01:11:37,833 --> 01:11:39,485
<i>We’ve been waiting for you here.</i>

991
01:11:40,402 --> 01:11:41,832
<i>Hello sir, can you hear me?</i>

992
01:11:42,195 --> 01:11:43,922
- <i>Sir, I’m telling you...
- Where are you?</i>

993
01:11:44,342 --> 01:11:47,330
<i>I’m here at Gauri Ghat.
Can you come quickly?</i>

994
01:11:48,619 --> 01:11:50,158
[mysterious music playing]

995
01:11:58,911 --> 01:12:00,372
Look at her audacity!

996
01:12:01,177 --> 01:12:03,144
The moment I saw her, I knew...

997
01:12:03,145 --> 01:12:05,379
I don't know where she went missing from.

998
01:12:05,722 --> 01:12:08,163
She probably cheated that man too.

999
01:12:08,164 --> 01:12:09,688
RANJITH: I very well know
how to manage a tour package.

1000
01:12:09,689 --> 01:12:11,760
They left us running around
while they went off having fun.

1001
01:12:11,761 --> 01:12:13,759
RANJITH: <i>Her phone is switched off.
I tried calling her.</i>

1002
01:12:13,995 --> 01:12:17,147
We came to Kashi looking for peace.

1003
01:12:17,564 --> 01:12:19,651
Now we've lost what little peace we had.

1004
01:12:19,886 --> 01:12:22,172
How would I... alone…? Hello?

1005
01:12:22,392 --> 01:12:24,017
Hello? I can hear you, go on.

1006
01:12:24,371 --> 01:12:25,378
Hello?

1007
01:12:26,474 --> 01:12:27,807
This isn’t going to end well.

1008
01:12:28,158 --> 01:12:30,558
Her sons said not to file a police case.

1009
01:12:30,559 --> 01:12:33,188
They said it’s fine
even if she never returns.

1010
01:12:33,189 --> 01:12:34,236
What a family!

1011
01:12:34,371 --> 01:12:36,340
She’s not her own son.
[Dog barks]

1012
01:12:36,784 --> 01:12:38,830
She can’t have children.

1013
01:12:39,365 --> 01:12:40,891
I said it from the begining.

1014
01:12:41,082 --> 01:12:43,608
Don’t take along someone cursed.

1015
01:12:43,609 --> 01:12:44,929
And here we are.

1016
01:12:46,009 --> 01:12:47,321
I’m telling you again,

1017
01:12:47,322 --> 01:12:49,361
If anything happens to her,
I’m not responsible.

1018
01:12:49,362 --> 01:12:50,808
You’ll have to deal with it.

1019
01:12:59,582 --> 01:13:00,589
Thank you.

1020
01:13:02,277 --> 01:13:03,363
[faint footsteps]

1021
01:13:03,714 --> 01:13:05,183
[indistinct chatter]

1022
01:13:06,863 --> 01:13:08,222
[sighs]

1023
01:13:10,597 --> 01:13:12,074
[vehicle passing]

1024
01:13:18,489 --> 01:13:19,496
Granny...

1025
01:13:19,894 --> 01:13:21,097
Hmm?

1026
01:13:21,792 --> 01:13:23,206
[indistinct chatter]

1027
01:13:24,269 --> 01:13:25,276
Hey!

1028
01:13:25,909 --> 01:13:26,915
What happened?

1029
01:13:27,602 --> 01:13:28,609
Tell me.

1030
01:13:33,152 --> 01:13:34,308
[slurping]

1031
01:13:34,914 --> 01:13:36,028
Why am I like this?

1032
01:13:38,461 --> 01:13:40,621
Honestly, I’m not like this.

1033
01:13:43,736 --> 01:13:44,742
Or maybe…

1034
01:13:47,302 --> 01:13:48,309
Maybe this is who I am.

1035
01:13:50,028 --> 01:13:51,122
And I’ll live like this.

1036
01:13:51,683 --> 01:13:53,130
Did anyone say don’t?

1037
01:13:55,171 --> 01:13:56,204
Yes.

1038
01:13:57,504 --> 01:13:58,881
They did.

1039
01:14:00,809 --> 01:14:03,509
Everyone said so, except him.

1040
01:14:03,910 --> 01:14:05,324
[soft melancholic music playing]

1041
01:14:06,562 --> 01:14:09,036
I don’t know who you are.

1042
01:14:10,489 --> 01:14:12,718
But the only reason
I’m talking to you this much

1043
01:14:12,719 --> 01:14:14,175
is because of him.

1044
01:14:19,129 --> 01:14:21,256
Is it wrong to speak like this?

1045
01:14:21,656 --> 01:14:22,878
Yes,

1046
01:14:23,010 --> 01:14:24,219
it is wrong.

1047
01:14:24,609 --> 01:14:27,413
Who am I to ask you?
Who are you to tell me?

1048
01:14:28,215 --> 01:14:29,698
Say nothing.
[Pigeons flutter]

1049
01:14:38,228 --> 01:14:39,235
It's okay, keep going!

1050
01:14:41,375 --> 01:14:42,749
Tell me, Leela.

1051
01:14:43,809 --> 01:14:45,046
Who is this “him”?

1052
01:14:45,236 --> 01:14:46,525
Your husband?

1053
01:14:51,752 --> 01:14:52,759
Master.

1054
01:14:53,526 --> 01:14:54,827
Who? Your teacher?

1055
01:14:55,439 --> 01:14:56,446
Yes.

1056
01:14:56,884 --> 01:14:58,979
Yes, a teacher.

1057
01:15:00,839 --> 01:15:02,946
He taught me what life is…

1058
01:15:04,159 --> 01:15:05,800
But I’m the one

1059
01:15:06,327 --> 01:15:08,260
who left him halfway.

1060
01:15:08,818 --> 01:15:09,885
Was it love?

1061
01:15:10,379 --> 01:15:11,412
No!

1062
01:15:11,639 --> 01:15:13,159
Nothing like that.

1063
01:15:13,926 --> 01:15:15,901
I saw him for the first time this morning.

1064
01:15:16,644 --> 01:15:18,362
[soft melancholic music continues]

1065
01:15:20,859 --> 01:15:22,314
Last night,

1066
01:15:22,642 --> 01:15:24,348
I came here with my team.

1067
01:15:25,519 --> 01:15:27,706
This morning, I got separated from them.

1068
01:15:28,212 --> 01:15:29,219
Separated?

1069
01:15:29,446 --> 01:15:31,204
Or did you walk away on purpose?

1070
01:15:31,806 --> 01:15:34,012
- Yes!
- Huh? Really?!

1071
01:15:34,456 --> 01:15:35,753
[soft pleasant music playing]

1072
01:15:36,126 --> 01:15:37,524
Speak straight, Leela.

1073
01:15:37,939 --> 01:15:40,071
I can’t stand this beating around the bush.

1074
01:15:52,192 --> 01:15:54,122
There’s a little girl Leela inside me.

1075
01:15:55,946 --> 01:15:58,159
I often talk to her.

1076
01:15:59,746 --> 01:16:03,812
No matter what I ask or say,
she keeps crying.

1077
01:16:05,812 --> 01:16:07,992
I feel like asking why she cries.

1078
01:16:10,719 --> 01:16:13,926
But I never once asked her.

1079
01:16:18,839 --> 01:16:21,454
Because I already know her answer.

1080
01:16:22,613 --> 01:16:24,464
[soft melancholic music playing]

1081
01:16:24,946 --> 01:16:26,732
Then what could I say to her?

1082
01:16:29,666 --> 01:16:32,286
“Live the life you always wished for”?

1083
01:16:33,545 --> 01:16:35,100
Should I say that?

1084
01:16:37,880 --> 01:16:40,206
Or should I tell her,

1085
01:16:40,792 --> 01:16:42,664
“This is your life, accept it.”

1086
01:16:44,386 --> 01:16:46,574
[music swells]

1087
01:16:51,085 --> 01:16:52,765
I have no one.

1088
01:16:54,992 --> 01:16:56,435
Only her.

1089
01:16:59,923 --> 01:17:01,412
Only her!

1090
01:17:04,646 --> 01:17:06,169
So today, for once,

1091
01:17:07,290 --> 01:17:09,210
I decided

1092
01:17:09,917 --> 01:17:12,190
she should live the life she wanted.

1093
01:17:14,712 --> 01:17:15,888
That’s why

1094
01:17:15,889 --> 01:17:17,762
I left my team behind.

1095
01:17:25,366 --> 01:17:26,963
I didn’t know what to do.

1096
01:17:29,305 --> 01:17:31,129
I lost my bag.

1097
01:17:32,726 --> 01:17:35,397
I was panicking, clueless.

1098
01:17:36,870 --> 01:17:38,245
[sighs]

1099
01:17:38,506 --> 01:17:40,298
That’s when Master came.

1100
01:17:43,529 --> 01:17:45,300
And I don’t even know why.

1101
01:17:50,132 --> 01:17:51,891
He probably didn’t come for me.

1102
01:17:53,692 --> 01:17:57,026
It felt like he came
for that little girl Leela.

1103
01:18:00,972 --> 01:18:01,995
But...

1104
01:18:02,295 --> 01:18:04,509
without realising that,

1105
01:18:05,228 --> 01:18:08,014
he pushed me back to my team again.

1106
01:18:12,552 --> 01:18:14,599
And that’s why…

1107
01:18:28,652 --> 01:18:29,863
[bangles jingling softly]

1108
01:18:43,892 --> 01:18:45,966
Leela, you’re 'adipoli.'

1109
01:18:47,732 --> 01:18:48,798
What do you mean?

1110
01:18:48,799 --> 01:18:50,311
I mean, you’re super!

1111
01:18:53,632 --> 01:18:55,052
What’s this?

1112
01:18:55,339 --> 01:18:56,346
This?

1113
01:18:56,812 --> 01:18:57,930
This ressembles my life.

1114
01:18:58,452 --> 01:19:00,284
Just going around in circles.

1115
01:19:00,285 --> 01:19:02,073
[pigeons fluttering]
[traffic noise]

1116
01:19:02,839 --> 01:19:03,910
That’s how it is.

1117
01:19:04,125 --> 01:19:05,365
It slips and falls in between.

1118
01:19:05,366 --> 01:19:07,659
I'll take it and spin it again.

1119
01:19:07,886 --> 01:19:10,559
It’s a loop. You wouldn’t get it.

1120
01:19:12,211 --> 01:19:14,244
Oh, yeah,
for now, your episode is running, right?

1121
01:19:15,755 --> 01:19:17,627
Come on, it's almost time for the Aarti.

1122
01:19:17,929 --> 01:19:19,766
We’ve got to find your master, right?

1123
01:19:20,480 --> 01:19:21,831
[footsteps]

1124
01:19:25,381 --> 01:19:27,435
But tell me, this “master”...

1125
01:19:28,415 --> 01:19:29,981
Does he have any bad habits?

1126
01:19:31,742 --> 01:19:32,808
Like?

1127
01:19:32,809 --> 01:19:35,156
Like smoking or drinking?

1128
01:19:35,255 --> 01:19:37,752
Oh no, I wouldn’t know that.

1129
01:19:38,582 --> 01:19:42,579
Really? You got so close to him
without knowing anything?

1130
01:19:45,342 --> 01:19:46,843
That’s why I said,

1131
01:19:47,037 --> 01:19:48,815
there’s nothing between us.

1132
01:19:48,816 --> 01:19:51,046
Hey, old-fashioned lady!

1133
01:19:51,529 --> 01:19:52,825
I'm talking about friendship.

1134
01:19:57,402 --> 01:19:59,148
[distant devotional music playing]

1135
01:19:59,149 --> 01:20:01,736
Friendship doesn’t need big things.

1136
01:20:02,362 --> 01:20:04,716
Just understand the little things,
that's all it takes.

1137
01:20:05,995 --> 01:20:07,477
Wow, well said!

1138
01:20:10,564 --> 01:20:12,322
Where are you from?

1139
01:20:12,962 --> 01:20:14,530
At presenst, this is my home.

1140
01:20:16,894 --> 01:20:17,949
[traffic noise]

1141
01:20:20,696 --> 01:20:22,305
And if he’s not there?

1142
01:20:23,135 --> 01:20:24,853
If he’s not there,

1143
01:20:24,854 --> 01:20:26,795
he’ll come to see you off at the station.

1144
01:20:26,796 --> 01:20:27,802
Not a chance.

1145
01:20:28,929 --> 01:20:31,238
I left him halfway, remember?

1146
01:20:31,668 --> 01:20:33,835
He must be mad at me.

1147
01:20:35,942 --> 01:20:36,949
He won’t come.

1148
01:20:38,047 --> 01:20:39,053
It’ll be fine.

1149
01:20:39,515 --> 01:20:40,849
I’m here, right?

1150
01:20:44,183 --> 01:20:45,449
[man humming]

1151
01:20:46,075 --> 01:20:47,081
HEY!

1152
01:20:47,622 --> 01:20:48,628
My bag!

1153
01:20:50,347 --> 01:20:51,683
[tense music playing]

1154
01:20:52,722 --> 01:20:53,847
[rapid footsteps]

1155
01:21:00,875 --> 01:21:02,119
- HEY!
- Hey, Leela!

1156
01:21:02,661 --> 01:21:03,668
Leela...

1157
01:21:06,424 --> 01:21:08,442
Hey! Hey! Get off!

1158
01:21:09,761 --> 01:21:11,347
[iron gate creaking]

1159
01:21:14,369 --> 01:21:15,375
Leela!

1160
01:21:15,629 --> 01:21:16,636
Hey!

1161
01:21:16,822 --> 01:21:17,829
Hey!

1162
01:21:21,795 --> 01:21:23,127
Where did he go?

1163
01:21:23,128 --> 01:21:23,894
[children chattering]

1164
01:21:23,895 --> 01:21:25,570
Leela, wait! I’ll come too.

1165
01:21:26,339 --> 01:21:27,855
[panting]

1166
01:21:35,917 --> 01:21:37,370
[music fades]

1167
01:21:38,027 --> 01:21:39,433
[panting]

1168
01:21:43,495 --> 01:21:45,206
[soothing music playing]

1169
01:21:48,683 --> 01:21:50,081
[footsteps]
[panting]

1170
01:21:55,721 --> 01:21:57,487
Where the hell were you?

1171
01:21:57,488 --> 01:21:58,706
Look at her!

1172
01:21:58,707 --> 01:22:00,215
They all came after me

1173
01:22:00,216 --> 01:22:02,151
Yeah, just blame me for bringing you here!

1174
01:22:02,152 --> 01:22:03,760
Why was your phone off?

1175
01:22:03,761 --> 01:22:04,871
Where's your phone, madam?

1176
01:22:04,872 --> 01:22:06,181
Why are you standing there like a statue?

1177
01:22:06,517 --> 01:22:07,838
[murmuring]

1178
01:22:10,166 --> 01:22:12,549
Did you come along
just to make our lives miserable?

1179
01:22:12,550 --> 01:22:13,963
Her damn phone's switched off.

1180
01:22:18,535 --> 01:22:19,542
Look at her!

1181
01:22:22,820 --> 01:22:24,716
Isn’t the train tomorrow morning?

1182
01:22:25,216 --> 01:22:26,222
What?

1183
01:22:26,436 --> 01:22:27,442
She’ll be there.

1184
01:22:28,033 --> 01:22:29,252
[bangles jingling]

1185
01:22:29,681 --> 01:22:31,314
[warm, soothing music playing]

1186
01:22:39,416 --> 01:22:40,791
[music swells]

1187
01:22:54,900 --> 01:22:56,377
[music fades]

1188
01:22:57,424 --> 01:22:58,752
[pigeons fluttering]

1189
01:23:02,482 --> 01:23:04,801
I didn’t do it intentionally.

1190
01:23:06,742 --> 01:23:07,749
I know.

1191
01:23:08,816 --> 01:23:10,587
They won't treat you well.

1192
01:23:14,669 --> 01:23:16,176
Why did you do all this?

1193
01:23:18,982 --> 01:23:21,055
Why did you leave me and go?

1194
01:23:23,424 --> 01:23:24,994
[soft music playing]

1195
01:23:26,338 --> 01:23:27,428
[footsteps approaching]

1196
01:23:27,429 --> 01:23:29,054
What's here, a new episode?

1197
01:23:32,696 --> 01:23:33,702
Master?

1198
01:23:34,622 --> 01:23:35,629
Hi, Master.

1199
01:23:36,209 --> 01:23:37,215
I am Shetty.

1200
01:23:41,209 --> 01:23:42,964
You’re Malayali, right?

1201
01:23:43,182 --> 01:23:44,236
So, how are you?

1202
01:23:46,915 --> 01:23:48,252
I’m Leela’s new friend.

1203
01:23:51,355 --> 01:23:53,731
I had promised Leela

1204
01:23:53,732 --> 01:23:55,514
I’d track you down and bring you.

1205
01:23:56,282 --> 01:23:57,359
But no worries.

1206
01:23:59,702 --> 01:24:02,171
What? Where have you been?

1207
01:24:02,172 --> 01:24:04,120
I've been looking for you the whole morning!

1208
01:24:04,357 --> 01:24:06,068
What? What are you doing here?

1209
01:24:06,069 --> 01:24:08,858
- Sorry, sorry. I’ll explain to you.
- I’m leaving tomorrow. You know that, right?

1210
01:24:08,859 --> 01:24:09,921
Yes, yes!

1211
01:24:09,922 --> 01:24:12,260
- I will explain, I will explain.
- No! No excuses.

1212
01:24:13,047 --> 01:24:14,407
Listen to me. Wait.

1213
01:24:14,408 --> 01:24:15,961
Listen! Come.

1214
01:24:16,885 --> 01:24:18,111
[playful music playing]

1215
01:24:18,755 --> 01:24:20,189
- Wait. Wait a second, okay?
- What?

1216
01:24:25,119 --> 01:24:26,233
Here’s your phone.

1217
01:24:26,234 --> 01:24:28,672
It’s short of 200 bucks,
I gave it to that thief.

1218
01:24:29,814 --> 01:24:30,861
Poor guy has to live too.

1219
01:24:30,947 --> 01:24:32,166
Okay, Master, I’m off.

1220
01:24:32,167 --> 01:24:33,198
Bye.

1221
01:24:33,199 --> 01:24:34,415
Have fun, guys.

1222
01:24:34,752 --> 01:24:36,213
[rapid footsteps]

1223
01:24:40,314 --> 01:24:41,525
[pigeons fluttering]

1224
01:24:52,721 --> 01:24:54,062
I feel a bit tired.

1225
01:24:55,202 --> 01:24:56,893
I feel like freshening up.

1226
01:24:57,442 --> 01:25:00,226
If you don't mind, my hotel is nearby.

1227
01:25:01,222 --> 01:25:03,494
We can freshen up and then go for aarati.

1228
01:25:05,697 --> 01:25:06,830
[gentle music playing]

1229
01:25:07,682 --> 01:25:08,688
Okay.

1230
01:25:09,548 --> 01:25:10,602
Okay.

1231
01:25:15,799 --> 01:25:17,025
[scooter approaching]

1232
01:25:27,908 --> 01:25:29,181
[giggles]

1233
01:25:31,704 --> 01:25:33,184
Something wrong...

1234
01:25:33,853 --> 01:25:35,322
[scooter engine revving]

1235
01:25:36,502 --> 01:25:38,111
[dance teacher calling out steps]

1236
01:25:40,236 --> 01:25:41,767
[door creaks open]

1237
01:25:45,348 --> 01:25:46,355
Come.

1238
01:25:53,263 --> 01:25:54,269
You may go freshen up.

1239
01:25:55,849 --> 01:25:57,959
No, I’ll freshen up later.

1240
01:25:58,242 --> 01:25:59,598
Can I take a bath then?

1241
01:25:59,701 --> 01:26:00,708
Okay.

1242
01:26:06,525 --> 01:26:07,791
[door shutting]

1243
01:26:15,478 --> 01:26:17,174
[phone ringing]

1244
01:26:23,635 --> 01:26:25,510
Janaki’s calling.

1245
01:26:26,169 --> 01:26:27,657
Can you answer it?

1246
01:26:34,757 --> 01:26:35,978
Hello.

1247
01:26:35,979 --> 01:26:36,975
<i>Hello.</i>

1248
01:26:37,362 --> 01:26:38,915
Your dad’s in the shower.

1249
01:26:38,916 --> 01:26:41,032
Shall I ask him to call back?

1250
01:26:42,341 --> 01:26:43,419
Hello.

1251
01:26:43,420 --> 01:26:44,480
Hi aunty.

1252
01:26:44,481 --> 01:26:45,488
This is Janaki.

1253
01:26:45,638 --> 01:26:46,754
[soft chuckle]

1254
01:26:46,755 --> 01:26:48,895
I know, your dad told me.

1255
01:26:48,896 --> 01:26:49,958
[pleasant music playing]

1256
01:26:50,126 --> 01:26:51,558
Is dad with you?

1257
01:26:52,099 --> 01:26:53,106
Yes.

1258
01:26:53,899 --> 01:26:55,465
Not sure what happened in between.

1259
01:26:55,466 --> 01:26:56,983
I’ll ask him later.

1260
01:26:57,939 --> 01:27:00,086
We all were really tensed.

1261
01:27:01,559 --> 01:27:03,061
I feel relieved now.

1262
01:27:06,492 --> 01:27:07,499
Aunty.

1263
01:27:07,772 --> 01:27:09,130
Yes, dear?

1264
01:27:10,201 --> 01:27:12,371
I want to see you once.

1265
01:27:12,372 --> 01:27:13,379
Is it possible?

1266
01:27:13,899 --> 01:27:15,235
Of course, you can.

1267
01:27:18,146 --> 01:27:19,502
Are you going for aarati?

1268
01:27:22,220 --> 01:27:24,479
Yes, we’ll leave in half an hour.

1269
01:27:26,279 --> 01:27:28,325
If you have anything troubling your heart,

1270
01:27:28,326 --> 01:27:29,561
pray sincerely.

1271
01:27:29,659 --> 01:27:30,967
It will surely work out.

1272
01:27:32,786 --> 01:27:33,792
Okay.

1273
01:27:34,739 --> 01:27:36,200
Then I’ll call back later.

1274
01:27:36,886 --> 01:27:37,892
Alright, dear.

1275
01:27:38,072 --> 01:27:39,734
And thank you.

1276
01:27:50,880 --> 01:27:52,318
[music swells]

1277
01:28:13,292 --> 01:28:14,299
What did she say?

1278
01:28:16,565 --> 01:28:18,437
She said she surely wants to see me.

1279
01:28:20,272 --> 01:28:21,914
Have you thought about

1280
01:28:21,915 --> 01:28:24,090
what to do
when you meet them tomorrow?

1281
01:28:24,779 --> 01:28:26,403
No, we’ll see then.

1282
01:28:28,732 --> 01:28:30,205
Then go freshen up.

1283
01:28:30,406 --> 01:28:31,661
It’s time for aarati.

1284
01:28:45,091 --> 01:28:47,052
[bangles jingling]

1285
01:28:49,666 --> 01:28:50,672
One moment…

1286
01:28:51,219 --> 01:28:52,226
Huh?

1287
01:28:53,039 --> 01:28:54,046
I need jasmine flowers.

1288
01:28:55,989 --> 01:28:57,200
[door creaks open]

1289
01:28:58,497 --> 01:28:59,669
[door shutting]

1290
01:29:00,570 --> 01:29:01,985
[soft romantic music playing]

1291
01:29:07,064 --> 01:29:09,170
[song begins]

1292
01:29:16,822 --> 01:29:26,550
<i>♪ The dreams I thought were lost
are taking shape again ♪</i>

1293
01:29:26,679 --> 01:29:36,168
<i>♪ All that I believed had left me return,
like wings unfolding ♪</i>

1294
01:29:37,241 --> 01:29:46,276
<i>♪ Within these new desires,
life I thought was gone breathes once more ♪</i>

1295
01:29:46,869 --> 01:29:51,136
<i>♪ This is enough ♪</i>

1296
01:29:51,634 --> 01:29:56,487
<i>♪ My heart feels complete ♪</i>

1297
01:30:21,180 --> 01:30:31,503
<i>♪ I searched for myself in silence
and wandered in dark ♪</i>

1298
01:30:32,402 --> 01:30:40,755
<i>♪ Then you arrived,
and I found a gentle guardian in you ♪</i>

1299
01:30:41,159 --> 01:30:46,023
<i>♪ Who are you, and who am I, in this space? ♪</i>

1300
01:30:46,024 --> 01:30:50,378
<i>♪ The bond between us escapes every name ♪</i>

1301
01:30:51,110 --> 01:30:56,019
<i>♪ An unseen force weaves a secret lock
between us ♪</i>

1302
01:30:56,020 --> 01:31:00,209
<i>♪ And who holds the key to unfasten it? ♪</i>

1303
01:31:01,114 --> 01:31:10,276
<i>♪ I sense you in the wind
that brushes against me ♪</i>

1304
01:31:10,437 --> 01:31:19,995
<i>♪ When you are here, I need no one else ♪</i>

1305
01:31:19,996 --> 01:31:29,130
<i>♪ I want to journey far with you,
beneath an endless blue sky ♪</i>

1306
01:31:30,023 --> 01:31:34,807
<i>♪ This is enough ♪</i>

1307
01:31:34,808 --> 01:31:39,121
<i>♪ My heart feels complete ♪</i>

1308
01:31:39,586 --> 01:31:43,979
<i>♪ This is enough ♪</i>

1309
01:31:44,381 --> 01:31:49,177
<i>♪ My heart feels complete ♪</i>

1310
01:32:11,931 --> 01:32:13,877
[ambient noise at ghat]

1311
01:32:15,398 --> 01:32:17,054
That wasn't necessary.

1312
01:32:18,217 --> 01:32:19,444
What do you mean?

1313
01:32:20,476 --> 01:32:21,726
You paying them.

1314
01:32:22,241 --> 01:32:23,913
Just consider it as a form of art.

1315
01:32:25,954 --> 01:32:28,501
Then consider it as a ticket
to see the art.

1316
01:32:34,565 --> 01:32:36,894
Do you not believe in God?

1317
01:32:38,812 --> 01:32:41,592
[man singing]

1318
01:32:46,495 --> 01:32:48,127
Can I ask you something?

1319
01:32:49,011 --> 01:32:51,204
[mellow music playing]

1320
01:32:53,714 --> 01:32:55,464
You had a love marriage, I guess?

1321
01:32:55,884 --> 01:32:56,978
Yes.

1322
01:32:57,239 --> 01:32:59,497
Four years of love.

1323
01:33:02,411 --> 01:33:05,098
I've heard that
being in love feels so beautiful.

1324
01:33:06,845 --> 01:33:08,783
Why? Have you never been in love?

1325
01:33:10,761 --> 01:33:11,870
Sister...

1326
01:33:13,345 --> 01:33:14,767
Hey! Come here.

1327
01:33:16,023 --> 01:33:18,389
- Yes, sister.
- I was looking for you!

1328
01:33:18,621 --> 01:33:20,191
I want all of this.

1329
01:33:24,512 --> 01:33:27,932
[soft melodious music playing]

1330
01:33:46,304 --> 01:33:47,539
Can you please come here?

1331
01:33:50,872 --> 01:33:52,122
Hold this.

1332
01:33:52,498 --> 01:33:53,857
Okay.

1333
01:34:18,993 --> 01:34:21,086
[soft music playing]

1334
01:34:36,606 --> 01:34:38,965
One should visit this place
during the 'Dev Diwali' festival.

1335
01:34:40,594 --> 01:34:41,797
What's that?

1336
01:34:41,942 --> 01:34:45,231
On the fifteenth day of Diwali,
the full-moon night,

1337
01:34:45,544 --> 01:34:49,114
the whole Varanasi gets lit up
with lamps like this.

1338
01:34:50,246 --> 01:34:52,113
It's a delight to watch.

1339
01:34:53,952 --> 01:34:56,866
Please don't awaken my desires
by saying such things.

1340
01:34:58,211 --> 01:35:01,727
I'll feel bad when I realize that
I won't be able to do it.

1341
01:35:02,081 --> 01:35:04,648
Why do you have to feel bad?
You just need to come see the festival.

1342
01:35:06,348 --> 01:35:08,169
How can I come alone?

1343
01:35:17,520 --> 01:35:21,262
When auntie went missing,
it was like dad got stuck.

1344
01:35:21,434 --> 01:35:23,262
I've never seen dad like this.

1345
01:35:23,777 --> 01:35:26,988
I could feel the change in his voice
when I talked to him a moment ago.

1346
01:35:27,340 --> 01:35:29,035
He's happy with her.

1347
01:35:29,512 --> 01:35:30,605
<i>Come on, stop it!</i>

1348
01:35:30,910 --> 01:35:33,637
<i>Are you saying that he's fallen in love
at this age?</i>

1349
01:35:34,392 --> 01:35:36,915
Why not?
Why can't he fall in love at this age?

1350
01:35:37,082 --> 01:35:38,246
<i>I didn't mean it.</i>

1351
01:35:38,622 --> 01:35:39,832
Just think about it.

1352
01:35:39,833 --> 01:35:42,606
Dad being stubborn about
not coming with us to the U.K.,

1353
01:35:42,770 --> 01:35:44,747
and now him meeting this auntie,

1354
01:35:45,020 --> 01:35:46,894
isn't this all a coincidence?

1355
01:35:46,895 --> 01:35:48,599
<i>Whatever! Coincidence!</i>

1356
01:35:48,858 --> 01:35:50,606
<i>First, go meet auntie tomorrow.</i>

1357
01:35:50,903 --> 01:35:52,138
<i>Let's see after that.</i>

1358
01:35:53,036 --> 01:35:54,341
There's nothing to see here.

1359
01:35:54,661 --> 01:35:56,052
My mind is telling me that

1360
01:35:56,591 --> 01:35:58,106
this is something special.

1361
01:36:00,114 --> 01:36:01,232
Let it be.

1362
01:36:01,233 --> 01:36:02,848
Aren't you going to see the flat tomorrow?

1363
01:36:02,849 --> 01:36:04,810
<i>Oh, yes. Please be free tomorrow.</i>

1364
01:36:05,020 --> 01:36:06,317
<i>I'll facetime you.</i>

1365
01:36:06,481 --> 01:36:07,777
Okay.

1366
01:36:08,364 --> 01:36:09,980
<i>Call me after meeting auntie tomorrow.</i>

1367
01:36:09,981 --> 01:36:12,653
<i>I too wanna know
if Madhavan master is in love.</i>

1368
01:36:13,229 --> 01:36:15,161
Okay. Good night then.

1369
01:36:15,712 --> 01:36:17,080
Sorry, good noon.

1370
01:36:17,231 --> 01:36:19,247
<i>- Okay. Bye.</i>
- Bye.

1371
01:36:32,276 --> 01:36:34,901
Do you wanna buy anything for anybody?
You won't get time in the morning.

1372
01:36:37,221 --> 01:36:39,252
Who do I even have?

1373
01:36:40,237 --> 01:36:42,565
Isn't tomorrow Janaki's birthday?

1374
01:36:42,705 --> 01:36:44,682
Let's buy something for her.

1375
01:36:46,190 --> 01:36:48,877
She said she'll come here
tomorrow morning at 8.

1376
01:36:48,987 --> 01:36:50,948
She said we'll have breakfast together.

1377
01:36:53,112 --> 01:36:54,408
You want more chutney?

1378
01:36:55,291 --> 01:36:56,377
Brother...

1379
01:36:57,228 --> 01:36:58,284
Chutney.

1380
01:36:58,285 --> 01:36:59,612
Okay. One moment.

1381
01:36:59,823 --> 01:37:01,369
The chutney isn't that good.

1382
01:37:08,455 --> 01:37:09,877
It's really not good.

1383
01:37:10,721 --> 01:37:12,080
Visit Tanjavur sometime.

1384
01:37:12,362 --> 01:37:14,455
I'll make you nice dosas and chutney.

1385
01:37:16,752 --> 01:37:18,384
- Tamil?
- Yes!

1386
01:37:18,385 --> 01:37:19,432
Rajinikanth?

1387
01:37:20,783 --> 01:37:22,909
Thalaivar? Super, super!

1388
01:37:22,910 --> 01:37:24,174
Which movie do you like?

1389
01:37:25,033 --> 01:37:26,229
I don't know much Tamil.

1390
01:37:26,737 --> 01:37:28,307
Only Rajinikanth.

1391
01:37:31,440 --> 01:37:34,971
♪ Lungi dance, lungi dance ♪

1392
01:37:35,727 --> 01:37:37,440
[background applause]

1393
01:37:42,369 --> 01:37:44,229
When will you go back to your hometown?

1394
01:37:44,815 --> 01:37:46,143
In a couple of days.

1395
01:37:49,666 --> 01:37:51,174
Will you come with me?

1396
01:37:54,862 --> 01:37:56,158
I was just kidding.

1397
01:37:57,448 --> 01:38:00,698
If my travel group speaks bad about me
tomorrow,

1398
01:38:00,932 --> 01:38:04,940
I felt it'd be good if there's someone
who I can share it with.

1399
01:38:07,862 --> 01:38:10,744
Aren't we going back to the hotel
after food? I shall book another room.

1400
01:38:11,783 --> 01:38:13,205
No need.

1401
01:38:13,817 --> 01:38:16,549
I wish to stay at the ghat
throughout this night.

1402
01:38:37,882 --> 01:38:39,788
[pleasant music playing]

1403
01:38:42,527 --> 01:38:44,933
Never in my wildest dreams did I expect
all these to happen.

1404
01:39:18,265 --> 01:39:20,164
[flute playing]

1405
01:39:33,131 --> 01:39:35,241
Thank you. Thank you.

1406
01:39:37,824 --> 01:39:39,668
I have a small wish.

1407
01:39:42,176 --> 01:39:43,863
Dance...

1408
01:39:44,363 --> 01:39:46,410
[audience chattering]

1409
01:39:52,844 --> 01:39:55,070
[soft music playing]

1410
01:40:11,027 --> 01:40:12,356
This is Leela,

1411
01:40:12,357 --> 01:40:15,427
the beautiful dancer from Tamil Nadu.

1412
01:40:16,020 --> 01:40:18,270
She is gonna dance for us.

1413
01:40:18,763 --> 01:40:20,083
Leela, come.

1414
01:40:20,207 --> 01:40:21,402
Please. Come, come.

1415
01:40:22,137 --> 01:40:23,426
Hey, come on.

1416
01:40:23,715 --> 01:40:25,043
Just some small movements.

1417
01:40:30,434 --> 01:40:31,645
Please go ahead.

1418
01:40:42,547 --> 01:40:44,860
[flute playing]

1419
01:42:18,343 --> 01:42:20,630
[applause]

1420
01:42:35,068 --> 01:42:36,592
Thank you.

1421
01:42:37,888 --> 01:42:39,513
Leela, please come here.

1422
01:42:41,584 --> 01:42:43,037
Please come here.

1423
01:42:44,840 --> 01:42:46,036
Come. Come.

1424
01:42:53,068 --> 01:42:55,599
This is for you. Please.
Take it.

1425
01:42:56,390 --> 01:42:58,083
[soft music playing]

1426
01:43:06,313 --> 01:43:07,352
Let's go.

1427
01:43:08,139 --> 01:43:09,409
- Bye.
- Bye.

1428
01:43:17,727 --> 01:43:18,922
Thank you.

1429
01:43:24,421 --> 01:43:26,952
If I give you something,
will you accept it?

1430
01:43:27,594 --> 01:43:29,867
You've become quite rich, aren't you?

1431
01:43:32,227 --> 01:43:33,352
It's not like that.

1432
01:43:33,661 --> 01:43:35,161
This is my first salary.

1433
01:43:37,629 --> 01:43:39,020
Please keep it.

1434
01:43:40,034 --> 01:43:42,932
I'd rather prefer you buying me something.

1435
01:43:50,590 --> 01:43:53,075
I really miss my father today.

1436
01:43:54,559 --> 01:43:57,637
He was the one
who always supported my dance.

1437
01:43:58,133 --> 01:44:01,480
[melodious music playing]

1438
01:44:12,489 --> 01:44:14,340
What's happening there?

1439
01:44:15,770 --> 01:44:17,793
Oh, that?
It's the dead bodies being cremated.

1440
01:44:19,114 --> 01:44:20,731
Why didn't we go there?

1441
01:44:22,864 --> 01:44:24,411
Ever since Latha left me,

1442
01:44:24,903 --> 01:44:27,012
the sight of pyres burning scares me.

1443
01:44:32,817 --> 01:44:35,028
What will you do after going back home?

1444
01:44:36,567 --> 01:44:38,067
Janaki is also coming with me.

1445
01:44:38,981 --> 01:44:40,840
She must be having some plans.

1446
01:44:41,090 --> 01:44:43,387
She's planning to travel to the U.K.
after her course.

1447
01:44:44,028 --> 01:44:46,489
She's planning to launch dance classes there.

1448
01:44:47,137 --> 01:44:50,129
They're adamant about taking me along.

1449
01:44:50,778 --> 01:44:52,973
Alex called me and discussed about it
even yesterday.

1450
01:44:55,843 --> 01:44:57,202
Will you go with them?

1451
01:44:58,192 --> 01:45:00,272
[soft music playing]

1452
01:45:04,030 --> 01:45:06,093
It is quite difficult to live all by yourself.

1453
01:45:07,921 --> 01:45:10,054
It's better for you to go with Janaki.

1454
01:45:10,484 --> 01:45:14,464
[man singing]
[Man singing a song]

1455
01:45:25,241 --> 01:45:26,351
Who is this?

1456
01:45:30,226 --> 01:45:31,734
Master ji...

1457
01:45:32,101 --> 01:45:35,365
Isn't she the one who was crying at the store
in the morning?

1458
01:45:35,366 --> 01:45:37,187
Yes, she's the one!

1459
01:45:37,937 --> 01:45:39,898
And you're smiling now?

1460
01:45:40,413 --> 01:45:43,085
Something's fishy, Master ji!

1461
01:45:45,413 --> 01:45:46,882
Don't you wanna go home?

1462
01:45:47,554 --> 01:45:48,655
Home...

1463
01:45:51,991 --> 01:45:54,351
Master ji, the tunes of the waves...

1464
01:45:55,804 --> 01:45:57,890
The calling of the shores...

1465
01:45:59,155 --> 01:46:00,898
the kick of the booze...

1466
01:46:01,968 --> 01:46:04,382
and the elegance of the moonlight.

1467
01:46:05,241 --> 01:46:07,030
This is my home, Master ji.

1468
01:46:07,589 --> 01:46:09,292
This is all I have.

1469
01:46:09,546 --> 01:46:12,187
Or, you should have someone

1470
01:46:13,711 --> 01:46:15,375
who you can call your own.

1471
01:46:15,476 --> 01:46:17,827
No. She will go back tomorrow morning.

1472
01:46:18,054 --> 01:46:19,086
Why?

1473
01:46:20,821 --> 01:46:23,562
Did I say anything wrong, sister?

1474
01:46:26,202 --> 01:46:27,601
I see!

1475
01:46:27,866 --> 01:46:29,546
Please have it, sister.

1476
01:46:33,702 --> 01:46:36,226
I didn't understand anything you said.

1477
01:46:37,124 --> 01:46:38,523
But today, for this one day,

1478
01:46:38,835 --> 01:46:40,296
I've been living as myself.

1479
01:46:41,710 --> 01:46:44,046
He is not the only reason for that.

1480
01:46:44,687 --> 01:46:46,054
Even you are a reason for that.

1481
01:46:47,616 --> 01:46:48,913
Thanks a lot.

1482
01:46:50,351 --> 01:46:51,499
Madam...

1483
01:46:51,851 --> 01:46:53,140
I don't understand

1484
01:46:53,507 --> 01:46:55,296
your language.

1485
01:46:56,741 --> 01:46:58,937
But, there's a story about Varanasi.

1486
01:46:59,718 --> 01:47:02,507
Whoever comes here, Madam ji...

1487
01:47:03,445 --> 01:47:08,327
they leave something close to their heart
here in Varanasi.

1488
01:47:08,968 --> 01:47:10,421
But now, Madam ji...

1489
01:47:10,593 --> 01:47:12,359
he's doing just the opposite!

1490
01:47:13,788 --> 01:47:15,030
Master ji...

1491
01:47:16,437 --> 01:47:18,609
You're extremely lucky.

1492
01:47:22,280 --> 01:47:24,023
Did you understand what he said?

1493
01:47:24,943 --> 01:47:26,990
The people who come to Varanasi

1494
01:47:27,420 --> 01:47:30,290
usually leave behind something
close to their heart.

1495
01:47:30,291 --> 01:47:32,455
That's the custom here.

1496
01:47:34,034 --> 01:47:35,620
You have time till tomorrow, right?

1497
01:47:36,118 --> 01:47:37,369
Roam around more.

1498
01:47:37,370 --> 01:47:38,884
Go see the whole Varanasi.

1499
01:47:39,407 --> 01:47:40,766
Enjoy to the fullest!

1500
01:47:42,062 --> 01:47:43,090
Sure.

1501
01:47:45,399 --> 01:47:47,204
Praise, Lord Mahadev!

1502
01:47:47,205 --> 01:47:50,152
[soft music playing]

1503
01:47:52,971 --> 01:47:54,910
See how happy he is!

1504
01:47:54,911 --> 01:47:56,112
Yeah.

1505
01:47:56,921 --> 01:47:58,875
[giant wheel whirring in the background]

1506
01:48:08,513 --> 01:48:09,865
[playful music playing]

1507
01:48:11,341 --> 01:48:12,935
[giant wheel creaking]

1508
01:48:18,607 --> 01:48:20,201
[music swells]

1509
01:48:43,209 --> 01:48:44,404
[lip smacking]

1510
01:48:46,163 --> 01:48:49,770
You look just like a pre-school kid.

1511
01:48:50,350 --> 01:48:51,752
Why are you staring at me?

1512
01:48:52,303 --> 01:48:54,623
I saw you taking that woman to the lodge.

1513
01:48:57,443 --> 01:48:58,769
[giant wheel creaks to a stop]

1514
01:48:58,770 --> 01:49:00,903
Huh?! A new saree!

1515
01:49:02,077 --> 01:49:03,425
A new sweater too!

1516
01:49:05,977 --> 01:49:06,983
What’s the plan?

1517
01:49:07,663 --> 01:49:09,192
Is this train heading

1518
01:49:09,193 --> 01:49:11,241
to Thanjavur or to Kerala?

1519
01:49:18,160 --> 01:49:19,167
Give me money.

1520
01:49:19,294 --> 01:49:21,554
Little bro,
why do you need money?

1521
01:49:22,233 --> 01:49:24,327
They just bought new clothes.

1522
01:49:24,467 --> 01:49:26,660
Now they'll need to buy tickets home.

1523
01:49:26,767 --> 01:49:28,034
He’ll need money again anyway.

1524
01:49:28,146 --> 01:49:29,659
So, you pay him!

1525
01:49:31,068 --> 01:49:32,584
[playful music playing]

1526
01:49:37,154 --> 01:49:38,160
Give me money.

1527
01:49:38,488 --> 01:49:39,512
Huh?

1528
01:49:39,513 --> 01:49:40,909
Give me my money.

1529
01:49:42,627 --> 01:49:45,445
They rode the giant wheel,
why should I pay?

1530
01:49:45,446 --> 01:49:47,553
You’re the one who sent them! So, you pay.

1531
01:49:47,780 --> 01:49:50,730
You’re just a kid. Don’t talk too much.

1532
01:49:50,892 --> 01:49:51,920
Get lost.

1533
01:49:52,040 --> 01:49:53,080
Scram!

1534
01:49:53,607 --> 01:49:54,637
Scram!

1535
01:49:54,638 --> 01:49:55,984
He doesn't even know Hindi!

1536
01:49:55,985 --> 01:49:58,643
I’m holding my temper here
and he's bugging me for money?

1537
01:50:10,061 --> 01:50:11,787
I’ve never been

1538
01:50:12,973 --> 01:50:16,373
important in anyone’s life.

1539
01:50:17,189 --> 01:50:18,638
[soft, soothing music playing]

1540
01:50:18,867 --> 01:50:20,402
After all this,

1541
01:50:20,403 --> 01:50:23,592
didn’t you ever feel angry with the God?

1542
01:50:25,346 --> 01:50:26,699
I did.

1543
01:50:29,547 --> 01:50:30,554
Tell me.

1544
01:50:31,067 --> 01:50:33,571
What did you feel

1545
01:50:33,692 --> 01:50:35,325
when you first saw me?

1546
01:50:37,487 --> 01:50:39,900
Didn’t you suddenly cry
when I asked you the issue?

1547
01:50:41,319 --> 01:50:43,387
That moment, I thought,

1548
01:50:43,388 --> 01:50:45,177
“Oh, I’m trapped.”

1549
01:50:45,498 --> 01:50:47,599
[both laugh]

1550
01:50:48,640 --> 01:50:50,586
Ask me what I felt.

1551
01:50:52,090 --> 01:50:53,087
Um…

1552
01:50:53,960 --> 01:50:55,114
Ask me.

1553
01:50:55,254 --> 01:50:56,280
So, what was it?

1554
01:50:58,047 --> 01:50:59,260
Nothing at all.

1555
01:51:00,716 --> 01:51:02,201
[laughs]

1556
01:51:05,427 --> 01:51:06,753
But...

1557
01:51:07,697 --> 01:51:09,690
can I tell you what I feel now?

1558
01:51:13,994 --> 01:51:15,610
I’ve never

1559
01:51:16,971 --> 01:51:19,364
felt this way before, ever.

1560
01:51:25,400 --> 01:51:26,407
Truly.

1561
01:51:29,413 --> 01:51:31,244
It feels different.

1562
01:51:32,912 --> 01:51:34,146
[music swells]

1563
01:51:41,960 --> 01:51:45,878
Isn’t this wrong, at our age?

1564
01:51:46,453 --> 01:51:47,460
What?

1565
01:51:50,796 --> 01:51:53,466
Lying here stargazing with someone...

1566
01:51:55,788 --> 01:51:57,854
I just met this morning.

1567
01:52:01,584 --> 01:52:03,216
[laughs]

1568
01:52:04,650 --> 01:52:07,082
Do you think my husband, and your Latha,

1569
01:52:07,083 --> 01:52:09,805
are watching us from above?

1570
01:52:13,204 --> 01:52:18,444
Maybe smiling, seeing us together.

1571
01:52:26,091 --> 01:52:27,584
[music continues]

1572
01:52:28,897 --> 01:52:30,730
After Latha passed,

1573
01:52:30,817 --> 01:52:33,137
did you never fall in love again?

1574
01:52:35,021 --> 01:52:36,278
[both laugh]

1575
01:52:36,717 --> 01:52:38,220
See! That’s what I asked.

1576
01:52:38,221 --> 01:52:39,603
I thought so!

1577
01:52:42,853 --> 01:52:46,420
I've been craving for true love
all my life.

1578
01:52:46,841 --> 01:52:48,287
[soft music playing]

1579
01:52:48,840 --> 01:52:49,900
It’s okay.

1580
01:52:50,780 --> 01:52:52,052
I've aged, after all!

1581
01:52:57,514 --> 01:52:59,472
How were you when you were young?

1582
01:53:01,000 --> 01:53:02,564
When I was young…

1583
01:53:18,814 --> 01:53:19,820
You looked good.

1584
01:53:20,951 --> 01:53:22,448
No, not that good looking.

1585
01:53:24,037 --> 01:53:25,353
You lacked nothing.

1586
01:53:26,497 --> 01:53:28,843
Truly, you looked really good, master

1587
01:53:30,383 --> 01:53:31,845
Let me keep this with me.

1588
01:53:58,330 --> 01:53:59,912
What did you just pray for?

1589
01:54:01,471 --> 01:54:02,898
I can’t say that.

1590
01:54:04,150 --> 01:54:05,926
You’re already 53!

1591
01:54:06,350 --> 01:54:07,357
No.

1592
01:54:07,889 --> 01:54:08,896
52.

1593
01:54:09,307 --> 01:54:10,314
Oh.

1594
01:54:11,127 --> 01:54:14,195
Then shall I tell a story
to this 52-year-old kid?

1595
01:54:14,286 --> 01:54:15,395
Um…

1596
01:54:15,760 --> 01:54:19,000
Weren’t you about to tell me one
during breakfast?

1597
01:54:19,367 --> 01:54:20,374
Tell me that one.

1598
01:54:20,654 --> 01:54:21,749
Oh,

1599
01:54:21,750 --> 01:54:24,005
I felt so embarrassed then.

1600
01:54:25,034 --> 01:54:27,253
Of course! You had no sense at all.

1601
01:54:27,640 --> 01:54:29,476
I was so stressed,

1602
01:54:29,576 --> 01:54:31,676
and you chose that moment to tell me a story.

1603
01:54:32,521 --> 01:54:34,068
How could I listen?

1604
01:54:35,140 --> 01:54:36,444
That’s true.

1605
01:54:37,206 --> 01:54:38,213
So, tell it now.

1606
01:54:41,467 --> 01:54:43,102
I’m not in the mood.

1607
01:54:43,486 --> 01:54:44,619
Oh!

1608
01:54:45,099 --> 01:54:46,765
Is this revenge?

1609
01:54:46,766 --> 01:54:47,820
Yes, revenge.

1610
01:54:48,029 --> 01:54:49,670
[both laugh]

1611
01:54:51,754 --> 01:54:52,760
Come on, tell it.

1612
01:54:53,696 --> 01:54:55,299
Do you like listening to stories?

1613
01:54:55,467 --> 01:54:57,724
Um… I’ve loved them since childhood.

1614
01:54:57,725 --> 01:54:58,779
A lot!

1615
01:54:58,780 --> 01:55:03,787
Who told you stories as a child?
Your grandmother?

1616
01:55:04,411 --> 01:55:06,553
You said it right. Yes, my grandmother.

1617
01:55:06,833 --> 01:55:08,644
She told me so many stories.

1618
01:55:08,645 --> 01:55:10,900
I grew up listening to them all.

1619
01:55:11,339 --> 01:55:12,346
Oho!

1620
01:55:12,520 --> 01:55:13,579
Even now,

1621
01:55:13,580 --> 01:55:15,969
I remember every single one.

1622
01:55:16,294 --> 01:55:18,538
That’s how much I love stories.

1623
01:55:18,539 --> 01:55:21,621
That’s why I ask you for one too.

1624
01:55:21,814 --> 01:55:23,618
Tell me a story.

1625
01:55:23,619 --> 01:55:24,843
Alright then,

1626
01:55:24,844 --> 01:55:27,462
how about the story of two friends,
a mud ball and a dried leaf

1627
01:55:27,463 --> 01:55:29,057
who travelled to Kashi?

1628
01:55:29,058 --> 01:55:30,109
What's that story?

1629
01:55:30,110 --> 01:55:34,375
Well... A mud ball and a dried leaf
once planned to visit Kashi.

1630
01:55:34,376 --> 01:55:36,033
On their way,

1631
01:55:36,034 --> 01:55:37,608
a huge storm erupted.

1632
01:55:38,216 --> 01:55:40,466
[soft music playing]

1633
01:55:47,146 --> 01:55:48,599
[birds flapping wings]

1634
01:55:53,327 --> 01:55:54,835
[birds squawking]

1635
01:56:40,256 --> 01:56:41,858
[soft music playing]

1636
01:56:54,374 --> 01:56:55,663
[ambient noise]

1637
01:57:00,928 --> 01:57:02,233
[temple bell ringing]

1638
01:57:07,567 --> 01:57:08,574
Hello?

1639
01:57:09,994 --> 01:57:12,540
Aren’t you getting up?
It’s already morning.

1640
01:57:15,947 --> 01:57:16,954
We should leave, right??

1641
01:57:17,454 --> 01:57:18,460
Hello?

1642
01:57:19,706 --> 01:57:20,713
Leela…

1643
01:57:21,440 --> 01:57:22,447
Hey…

1644
01:57:27,627 --> 01:57:28,634
Hey, Leela…

1645
01:57:29,740 --> 01:57:30,747
Hey…

1646
01:57:32,659 --> 01:57:33,666
Leela…

1647
01:57:37,379 --> 01:57:38,386
Leela!

1648
01:57:39,734 --> 01:57:40,741
Leela!

1649
01:57:44,694 --> 01:57:46,311
[tense ambience builds]

1650
01:58:04,660 --> 01:58:06,092
Tea! Tea! Tea!

1651
01:58:06,093 --> 01:58:07,113
Sir, tea?

1652
01:58:07,327 --> 01:58:08,334
Hot tea!

1653
01:58:08,580 --> 01:58:10,323
Yes, two cups.

1654
01:58:16,823 --> 01:58:18,899
- Hey, tea seller.
- I’m coming.

1655
01:58:19,071 --> 01:58:20,187
Bring us some tea.

1656
01:58:26,655 --> 01:58:27,920
[soft melancholic music playing]

1657
01:58:38,006 --> 01:58:39,475
[somber music builds]

1658
01:59:29,749 --> 01:59:31,256
[indistinct chatter]

1659
01:59:39,350 --> 01:59:41,085
[music intensifies]

1660
02:01:02,960 --> 02:01:04,460
[music fades]

1661
02:01:18,389 --> 02:01:19,874
[somber music playing]

1662
02:01:37,357 --> 02:01:38,850
[fire crackling]

1663
02:01:39,686 --> 02:01:41,295
[somber music intensifies]

1664
02:02:21,936 --> 02:02:23,866
[ambient noise]

1665
02:02:42,845 --> 02:02:52,679
<i>♪ Like a fading lamp with a mystic glow ♪</i>

1666
02:02:53,115 --> 02:03:03,203
<i>♪ Like the mist that swallows the morning ♪</i>

1667
02:03:03,549 --> 02:03:13,474
<i>♪ Like the shadow of
a broken song someone hums ♪</i>

1668
02:03:13,868 --> 02:03:23,209
<i>♪ Like ripples born from an imagined boat ♪</i>

1669
02:03:24,076 --> 02:03:33,027
<i>♪ Who are you? Who are you? ♪</i>

1670
02:03:33,520 --> 02:03:39,220
<i>♪ So near, and yet beyond my reach ♪</i>

1671
02:03:39,510 --> 02:03:43,596
<i>♪ Who are you? ♪</i>

1672
02:03:49,766 --> 02:03:59,778
<i>♪ From a branch that touched the sky ♪</i>

1673
02:04:00,141 --> 02:04:09,702
<i>♪ Where did you fly, radiant little bird? ♪</i>

1674
02:04:09,950 --> 02:04:19,972
<i>♪ Without lingering a moment longer,
where did you vanish? ♪</i>

1675
02:04:20,531 --> 02:04:30,741
<i>♪ Like a fading lamp with a mystic glow ♪</i>

1676
02:04:30,872 --> 02:04:40,590
<i>♪ Like the mist that swallows the morning ♪</i>

1677
02:04:41,212 --> 02:04:51,452
<i>♪ Like the rhythm of
a doomed song someone hums ♪</i>

1678
02:04:51,453 --> 02:04:56,256
<i>♪ Like a melody that stumbles in the wind ♪</i>

1679
02:04:56,257 --> 02:05:01,369
<i>♪ You dissolve into a dream ♪</i>

1680
02:05:01,827 --> 02:05:10,827
<i>♪ Who are you? ♪</i>

1681
02:05:11,240 --> 02:05:21,669
<i>♪ You drift, farther and farther away ♪</i>

1682
02:05:22,308 --> 02:05:31,450
<i>♪ Farther and farther away ♪</i>

